ht recolored)\n- Comp/Code Input (\"Code\" label + 4 boxes)\n- Comp/Button Secondary (364×67 white, border #E2E2E2, radius 19, text dark SemiBold 18 \"Back to home\")\n- Comp/Phone Field? decided: use given TextField on sign-in w/ overlay prefix. So no.\n- Comp/Screen Header (back circle + centered title + optional right circle?) — skip component; per-frame compose: back circle = Comp/Circle Button instance (with chevron-left). Create Comp/Circle Button: 44×44 white circle shadow + child icon instance chevron-left? Icons differ per use (back chevron-left, share, filter, close). Make Comp/Circle Button with chevron-left child; swap nested icon via swapComponent to an icon COMPONENT — but my SVG icons are plain frames, not components. To support swapping, make small icon components? That's heavy. Alternative: Circle Button without icon child; place SVG icon on top per frame (z-above circle instance). Acceptable — circle button reusable, glyph placed per use. But then glyph not part of component — fine.\n   Comp/Circle Button: 44×44, white, radius 22, shadow 0 2 8 rgba(0,0,0,0.12).\n- Comp/Tab Bar set (5 variants) — biggest one.\n- Also Comp/Checkout Row.\n- Comp/Heart Button? 06 favourite: Icon_Favourite recolored #B1B1B1, size 28. Just instance per frame; no component needed... make Comp/Favourite Button: 36×36 transparent, heart icon #B1B1B1 (not favourited state). One use only — skip component, direct instance.\n\nAlso Status Bar & Home Indicator & Button & TextField: given components (I have their IDs).\n\n**Call 2 — Frames 01-04** (Splash, Onboarding, Sign In, Verification).\n**Call 3 — Frame 05 Home**.\n**Call 4 — Frames 06, 07**.\n**Call 5 — Frames 08, 09**.\n**Call 6 — Frames 10, 11, 12**.\n**Call 7 — Prototype wiring**.\nThen screenshots & fixes.\n\nFrame naming must be EXACT: \"01_Splash\", \"02_Onboarding\", \"03_Sign_In\", \"04_Verification\", \"05_Home\", \"06_Product_Detail\", \"07_Explore\", \"08_Beverages\", \"09_My_Cart\", \"10_Checkout_Overlay\", \"11_Order_Accepted\", \"12_Account\".\n\nPositions in workspace:\nRow1 y=0: 01 x0, 02 x514, 03 x1028, 04 x1542\nRow2 y=1000: 05 x0 (h1348), 06 x514, 07 x1028, 08 x1542\nRow3 y=2450: 09 x0, 10 x514, 11 x1028, 12 x1542\nComponents section: x2200 y0: components laid out vertically with spacing; tab bar variants at y ~1200. I'll arrange: labels? Components don't need labels; place sequentially y += h + 40. I'll maintain cursor.\n\nPrototype reactions — set via node.reactions? Let me confirm plugin API: `node.reactions = [{ action: {...}, trigger: {...} }]` — hmm, I believe it's `node.reactions` — wait, actually I recall `prototypeReactions`? No... In Figma plugin API docs: \"reactions: ReadonlyArray<Reaction>\" on SceneNode (BaseNodeMixin? It's on DefaultShapeMixin? It's on `SceneNode` via `reactions` property — actually `reactions` is on `BaseNodeMixin`? Let me recall: InteractionSchema... The property `reactions` exists on FrameNode, ComponentNode, InstanceNode, TextNode etc. Setting node.reactions = [{ action: { type: \"NODE\", destinationId: \"5:2\", navigation: \"NAVIGATE\", transition: null, overlay: null }, trigger: { type: \"CLICK\" } }]. Yes I'm fairly confident: Reaction = { action, trigger }; NavigateAction = { type: \"NODE\", destinationId, navigation, transition, overlay? }. Trigger ClickTrigger = { type: \"CLICK\" }. AfterDelayTrigger = { type: \"AFTER_DELAY\", delay: 1000 }? I think it's {type: \"AFTER_DELAY\", delay: number} in ms.\n\nFlow starting point: frame.flowStartingPoint? Hmm — I don't think FrameNode has flowStartingPoint... Actually there IS: `node.flowStartingPoint`? I'm not sure. There's `figma.viewport`... Flow starting points: In plugin API, `FrameNode` has `flowStartingPoint: FlowStartingPoint | null`? I believe yes — FrameNode.flowStartingPoint exists (writable). I'll try; wrap in try/catch.\n\nAlso \"10_Checkout_Overlay opens over 09_My_Cart\" — as prototype, could use navigation \"OVERLAY\" but brief treats it as a frame with close → 09. The evaluation: links close→09, Place Order→11. I'll use NAVIGATE transitions for simplicity and reliability. For \"opens over\", the frame itself shows cart behind — satisfied visually.\n\nTransition: default instant (transition: null? Reaction requires transition maybe null allowed). I'll set transition: {type:\"SMART_ANIMATE\", easing, duration:300}? Keep null (instant) to avoid schema issues. Actually NavigationAction requires `transition` and `overlay`? Schema: NavigateAction { type:\"NODE\", destinationId, navigation, transition, overlay? }. I'll include transition: null and overlay: null? If overlay required for navigation OVERLAY only. I'll try with transition null; if error, adjust.\n\nText: set textAutoResize NONE w/ fixed sizes for centered? For centered text width 366 textAlignHorizontal CENTER with autoResize HEIGHT.\n\nLet me also double check Tab Bar icons: Icon_Explore 24×16 (wide), Icon_Account 20×24, Icon_Cart 24×22, Icon_Favourite 24×21, Icon_Shop 24×24. When centering, position by icon width: x = tabX + (82.8 - w)/2.\n\nColors for tab states: active icon+label #53B175; inactive #181725. \n\nLabels: Shop, Explore, Cart, Favourite, Account — Poppins Medium 11.\n\nLet me write Call 1 code. Keep under 50k chars. I'll be economical.\n\nHelper functions shared per call (redefine each call):\n\n```js\nconst F = (hex, o=1) => { const n=parseInt(hex.slice(1),16); return {type:\"SOLID\", color:{r:((n>>16)&255)/255, g:((n>>8)&255)/255, b:(n&255)/255}, opacity:o}; };\nconst C = { brand:\"#53B175\", dark:\"#181725\", gray:\"#7C7C7C\", light:\"#B1B1B1\", border:\"#E2E2E2\", surface:\"#F2F3F2\", white:\"#FFFFFF\", orange:\"#F3603F\", red:\"#EB5757\" };\nawait figma.loadFontAsync({family:\"Poppins\", style:\"Regular\"});\nawait figma.loadFontAsync({family:\"Poppins\", style:\"Medium\"});\nawait figma.loadFontAsync({family:\"Poppins\", style:\"SemiBold\"});\nawait figma.loadFontAsync({family:\"Poppins\", style:\"Bold\"});\nconst WS = figma.getNodeById(\"7:2\");\nconst getComp = id => figma.getNodeById(id);\nfunction txt(chars, size, style, color, w, x, y, align){ const t=figma.createText(); t.fontName={family:\"Poppins\",style}; t.characters=chars; t.fontSize=size; t.fills=[F(color)]; if(w){t.resize(w, t.height); t.textAutoResize=\"HEIGHT\";} if(align) t.textAlignHorizontal=align; if(x!==undefined){t.x=x;t.y=y;} return t; }\nfunction svgIcon(svg, name, size, color){ const n=figma.createNodeWithSvg(svg.replace(/__C__/g,color)); n.name=name; n.resize(size, size*(n.height/n.width)); ... }\n```\n\nHmm svg with stroke color param: svgIcon(svgStr, w, h, color) → createNodeWithSvg, then n.rescale? For stroke icons: viewBox 24, I pass width w height w. resize frame then children scale? Frame resize doesn't scale children. Use n.rescale(w / n.width) — rescale exists on nodes? `node.rescale(scale)` — yes, rescale(scale) exists on BaseNode (LayoutMixin.rescale). I'll use rescale.\n\nFor recolor: n.findAll(l => l.type===\"VECTOR\" || l.type===\"BOOLEAN_OPERATION\" ...). For stroke icons, vectors have strokes; set l.strokeStrokes? No: l.strokes=[F(color)].\n\nMedia instance helper:\n```js\nfunction media(id, w, parent, x, y){ const m = getComp(id).createInstance(); const ar = m.height/m.width; m.resize(w, w*ar); parent.appendChild(m); if(x!==undefined){m.x=x;m.y=y;} return m; }\n```\nFor fit-in-box (max W & H): compute scale = Math.min(maxW/mw, maxH/mh), resize(mw*s, mh*s).\n\nRecolor instance icon:\n```js\nfunction recolor(node, hex){ const c=F(hex); for (const l of node.findAll(l=>\"fills\" in l && l.fills && l.fills.length && l.type!==\"INSTANCE\"? false : false)) ... }\n```\nSimpler: findAll(l => l.type === \"VECTOR\" || l.type === \"ELLIPSE\" || l.type===\"RECTANGLE\" || l.type===\"TEXT\" || l.type===\"BOOLEAN_OPERATION\"), if l.fills && l.fills.length && l.fills[0].visible!==false → l.fills=[c]; if l.strokes && l.strokes.length && l.strokes[0].visible!==false → l.strokes=[c].\n\nCareful: Home Indicator's white bg frame: recolor should skip the frame bg? I handle statusbar recolor manually with children list.\n\nGiven Button instance:\n```js\nfunction brandButton(label, parent, x, y){ const b = getComp(\"6:29\").createInstance(); b.x=x; b.y=y; const t=b.children[0]; t.characters=label; parent.appendChild(b); return b; }\n```\nWait instance child text: b.findOne(n=>n.type===\"TEXT\"). Font already SemiBold 18 — override characters only.\n\nNow the Tab Bar variants. Build function makeTabBar(activeKey): frame 414×84 white; shadow; hairline top? Add stroke? I'll add top border via 1px rect #E2E2E2 at y0 width 414. Tabs array: [ [\"Shop\",\"4:163\",24,24], [\"Explore\",\"4:130\",24,16], [\"Cart\",\"4:121\",24,22], [\"Favourite\",\"4:136\",24,21], [\"Account\",\"4:118\",20,24] ]. tabW = 414/5 = 82.8. icon y = 18 + (24-ih)/2 center in 24 box at y18..42: icon x = tx + (82.8-24)/2 (center 24 box). label y 50, width 82.8 center align 11 Medium. Colors: active → brand, else dark.\nCreate 5 frames named \"ActiveTab=Shop\" etc., combineAsVariants(figma.combineAsVariants(nodes, WS)) → set.name=\"Tab Bar\". Then componentSet. Instance: compSet.defaultVariant? create instance via compSet.createInstance()? ComponentSetNode.createInstance? Hmm — ComponentSetNode doesn't have createInstance? Actually you create instance from one of its variants: compSet.children[i].createInstance(), then instance.setProperties({ActiveTab:\"Explore\"}). setProperties exists on InstanceNode. Good.\n\nEffects: shadow = {type:\"DROP_SHADOW\", color:{r:0,g:0,b:0,a:0.05}, offset:{x:0,y:-4}, radius:16, visible:true, blendMode:\"NORMAL\"}.\n\nHome Indicator on tab bar screens: place separate instance at bottom (bg white). Tab bar 84 + HI 34: total bottom chrome 118. In frames at H=896: tabbar y=778, HI y=862.\n\nFor Home (1348): tabbar y=1230, HI y=1314.\n\nProduct Card component (auto-layout vertical, 171 wide, padding 12, gap 0? custom gaps):\nchildren:\n- image frame 147×86 (clips false) — I'll place media instance centered in it (