components at x 2250.., y cursor. Also add a section label? Skip labels (text \"Components\" heading optional — add small text heading \"Components\" at 2250,0, and \"Screens\" heading? Screens have exact names required; adding extra heading frames is fine as long as 12 frames exist with exact names. I'll skip extra clutter; maybe one text \"Components\" for tidiness.)\n\nPrototype wiring (Call 7): map frames by name → id. For each link, find source node by path:\n- 01_Splash frame: after delay 1500 → 02.\n- 02: button instance (given Button, name it \"Get Started\") → 03.\n- 03: phone field group (frame \"Phone Field\" wrapping prefix + TF) → 04.\n- 04: back circle (name \"Back\") → 03; FAB (name \"Next\") → 05.\n- 05: Red Apple card instance → 06; tabbar instance: find tab node \"Explore\" → 07, \"Cart\" → 09, \"Account\" → 12.\n- 06: back → 05; button \"Add To Basket\" → 09.\n- 07: Beverages card → 08; tabbar: Shop→05, Cart→09, Account→12.\n- 08: back → 07.\n- 09: button → 10; tabbar: Shop→05, Explore→07, Account→12.\n- 10: close icon frame → 09; button → 11.\n- 11: secondary button \"Back to home\" → 05.\n- 12: tabbar: Shop→05, Explore→07, Cart→09.\n\nSet reactions on: for tab links, target node = the tab group frame inside the tabbar instance (findOne by name \"Tab/Explore\" etc.). Reactions can be set on instance children? Setting reactions on sublayers of instances — allowed? Prototype interactions on nested instance children: In Figma UI you CAN add interactions to nested elements. Plugin API: node.reactions settable on nodes inside instances? I believe yes (it's an override). Risk: might throw \"cannot set reactions on instance children\". Mitigation: set reactions on the TAB BAR instance's child tab frames — if fails, set on invisible hotspot rects placed on top of tabs in each screen frame (hotspot approach — always works). To be safe, plan hotspots: for each tab in each screen's tabbar, place a transparent rect (or use the tab label text?) — hotspot rects with fills [] inside screen frame above tabbar. That's 3 hotspots × 4 screens. Actually simplest uniform approach: for ALL links, place transparent \"hotspot\" rects/frames over the interactive areas (buttons, cards, tabs) named \"Hotspot/…\" and set reactions on those — avoids any instance-child issues for reactions. But reactions on the Button instance itself should be fine (top-level instance node). Product card instance → reactions fine. Only nested tab children are risky → hotspots there.\n\nAlso mark 01_Splash as flow starting point via try { frame.flowStartingPoint = {nodeId: frame.id, name: \"Nectar Shopper Flow\"} } catch(e){}.\n\nTransition: I'll use {type:\"SMART_ANIMATE\"?? } — for navigate transitions need easing/duration object: transition: { type: \"SMART_ANIMATE\", duration: 0.3, easing: {type:\"ease_out\"} }? Schema: Transition = {type:\"DISSOLVE\"|\"SMART_ANIMATE\"|\"MOVE_IN\"|\"MOVE_OUT\"|\"PUSH\"|\"SLIDE_IN\"|\"SLIDE_OUT\", duration: number (seconds), easing: Easing}. Easing {type:\"EASE_OUT\"}? Easing types: \"LINEAR\" | \"EASE_IN\" | \"EASE_OUT\" | \"EASE_IN_AND_OUT\" | \"CUSTOM...\" I'll use {type:\"SLIDE_IN\", direction:\"LEFT\"? } — keep simple: transition: {type:\"DISSOLVE\", duration:0.2, easing:{type:\"EASE_OUT\"}}? Hmm DISSOLVE for all. Or null for instant. Instant is safest & acceptable. I'll try SMART_ANIMATE 0.3 EASE_OUT; wrap each set in try/catch and fallback to transition:null.\n\nActually to minimize failure modes: first attempt with transition null (instant). Figma UI shows instant navigation — perfectly valid prototype.\n\nAfter-delay trigger on splash: trigger {type:\"AFTER_DELAY\", delay:2000}.\n\nNow write Call 1. Length concern: ~15-18k chars OK.\n\nOne more thing: fonts — \"Poppins\" must be available in Figma (Google font — yes). The given components use \"Poppins\" style \"SemiBold\" (note: statusBar text font \"Semi Bold\" reported for 9:41 — fontName.style \"Semi Bold\"?? The brief of button said style \"SemiBold\" and inspection shows \"SemiBold\". Status bar text style reported \"Semi Bold\" — inconsistent kit; whatever, I only set Poppins Regular/Medium/SemiBold/Bold myself.)\n\nLet me also confirm tab bar icon recoloring when instance inside variant component — components' children are normal nodes, recolor directly.\n\nMedia components are on \"Stage\"/\"tile\" pages (reference) — instantiating from them is reuse, allowed. Don't move them.\n\nWrite Call 1 now. I'll include a compact but complete script. I'll number components and return their IDs.\n\nAlso note: createNodeWithSvg — available in plugin API: figma.createNodeWithSvg(svg: string, normalizeOutput?: boolean?). Not in forbidden list. OK.\n\nStar SVG for review: fill color #F3603F — filled path with fill attr; recolor fills.\n\nCode for Call 1:\n\n```js\nawait Promise.all([[\"Regular\"],[\"Medium\"],[\"SemiBold\"],[\"Bold\"]].map(s=>figma.loadFontAsync({family:\"Poppins\",style:s[0]})));\nconst WS = figma.getNodeById(\"7:2\");\nconst F = (hex,o=1)=>{const n=parseInt(hex.slice(1),16);return {type:\"SOLID\",color:{r:((n>>16)&255)/255,g:((n>>8)&255)/255,b:(n&255)/255},opacity:o};};\nconst C={brand:\"#53B175\",dark:\"#181725\",gray:\"#7C7C7C\",light:\"#B1B1B1\",border:\"#E2E2E2\",surface:\"#F2F3F2\",white:\"#FFFFFF\",orange:\"#F3603F\"};\nconst K={}; // id map\nconst MASTER={}; // media masters by name\nfor(const c of figma.root.findAllWithCriteria({types:[\"COMPONENT\"]})) MASTER[c.name]=c;\n\nfunction txt(chars,size,style,color,x,y,w,align){const t=figma.createText();t.fontName={family:\"Poppins\",style};t.characters=chars;t.fontSize=size;t.fills=[F(color)];if(w){t.textAutoResize=\"HEIGHT\";t.resize(w,t.height);}if(align)t.textAlignHorizontal=align;if(x!==undefined){t.x=x;t.y=y;}return t;}\nfunction svgI(path,w,h,color,fillMode){const s=fillMode?`<svg width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><path d=\"${path}\" fill=\"${color}\"/></svg>`:`<svg width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><path d=\"${path}\" stroke=\"${color}\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/></svg>`;const n=figma.createNodeWithSvg(s);n.resize(w,h);... \n```\n\nHmm resize won't scale children. Use rescale: n.rescale(w/24)? svg frame is 24×24 given width/height attrs. n.rescale(w/24). For non-square (chevron w10 h16): rescale(10/24) → 10×10. Need stretch? Keep aspect (icons fine square-ish). I'll rescale to target width; height = 24*scale. For chevron-down in list rows use 12 wide → 12×12. OK.\n\nSimpler svgI(d, size, color, filled): rescale(size/24).\n\nfitBox(inst, maxW, maxH): compute from current inst.width/height (aspect preserved): s=Math.min(maxW/inst.width, maxH/inst.height); inst.resize(inst.width*s, inst.height*s).\n\nrecolorNode(n, hex): \n```js\nfunction recolorNode(n,hex){const c=[F(hex)];const walk=l=>{if(l.type===\"VECTOR\"||l.type===\"ELLIPSE\"||l.type===\"RECTANGLE\"||l.type===\"BOOLEAN_OPERATION\"||l.type===\"STAR\"||l.type===\"LINE\"){if(l.fills&&l.fills.length&&l.fills!==figma.mixed&&l.fills[0].visible!==false)l.fills=c;if(l.strokes&&l.strokes.length&&l.strokes!==figma.mixed&&l.strokes[0].visible!==false)l.strokes=c;}if(l.type===\"TEXT\"){l.fills=c;}if(\"children\"in l)l.children.forEach(walk);};walk(n);}\n```\nCareful: Circle button frame fill white would be recolored if passed — only pass icon nodes. For icon instances (media), their bg frames? Media icon components: master is symbol frame probably with no fill (transparent) — icon vectors inside. But Status Bar has white bg frame — recolor only specific children. OK.\n\nFor Tab Bar: I create icons as instances of media icon components, recolor via recolorNode(instance, color) — instance children vectors get overridden. \n\nProduct Card image default: instance of Product_Red_Apple.\n\nLet me now also define the media fit helper inside card component creation: the image child inside Product Card component is an INSTANCE of media comp — placed at computed center. In component: imgFrame (frame 147×86, fills[]) with child instance fit → center: x=(147-w)/2, y=(86-h)/2.\n\nPer-instance overrides in screens: cardInst.children — find name \"Image\" (I'll name the img container \"Image\", and inside instance child named \"Photo\") → cardInst.findOne(n=>n.name===\"Photo\") is the media instance → swapComponent(MASTER[name]) then refit: after swap, need refit inside Image frame: compute from MASTER dims: w=master.width*s... I'll write helper swapFit(photoInst, mediaName, maxW, maxH): photoInst.swapComponent(MASTER[mediaName]); const mw=MASTER[mediaName].width, mh=MASTER[mediaName].height; const s=Math.min(maxW/mw, maxH/mh); photoInst.resize(mw*s, mh*s); center within parent frame: photoInst.x=(photoInst.parent.width-photoInst.width)/2; photoInst.y=(photoInst.parent.height-photoInst.height)/2;\n\nWait — resize after swap: instance adopts master size on swap? Then I resize to fit. Fine.\n\nText overrides in card: findOne(n=>n.name===\"Name\").characters=..., \"Unit\", \"Price\".\n\nGood. Cart Item image: container frame \"Photo Box\" 70×70 with \"Photo\" instance fit 66.\n\nNow write everything. Also set WS as current page? Not needed; appendChild to WS works from any page? Creating nodes: figma.createFrame() adds to currentPage; then WS.appendChild(node) moves it. Fine.\n\nFor combineAsVariants: figma.combineAsVariants(nodes, WS, index?) → ComponentSetNode. Set name \"Tab Bar\".\n\nSet component descriptions? Optional; add brief descriptions to key components for polish. Skip to save space — maybe add for main ones quickly via comp.description = \"...\". I'll add a couple.\n\nAlso IMPORTANT: 03 Workspace page might need \"workspace\" naming of frames EXACT — yes.\n\nLet me also think about what could fail: text width override — after setting characters on overridden instance text with textAutoResize set on master, fine.\n\nAuto-layout product card: layoutMode=\"VE