{"type":"assistant","message":{"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me resume the work. I need to build the component library in 03 · Workspace. The last call failed due to input truncation, so I'll split into smaller calls.\n\nLet me start with Call 1a: helpers + first batch of components (Add Button, Quantity Stepper, Product Card, Search Bar, Section Header, Category Card, Category Chip).\n\nI need to be careful about the code size — keep it under ~8k characters.\n\nLet me write the code carefully. Key considerations:\n- Load fonts first\n- Get workspace node 7:2\n- Build components with exact names\n- Return JSON of created component IDs\n\nLet me draft Call 1a code:\n\n```js\nawait Promise.all([\"Regular\",\"Medium\",\"SemiBold\",\"Bold\"].map(s=>figma.loadFontAsync({family:\"Poppins\",style:s})));\nconst WS=figma.getNodeById(\"7:2\");\nconst F=(hex,o=1)=>{const n=parseInt(hex.slice(1),16);return{type:\"SOLID\",color:{r:((n>>16)&255)/255,g:((n>>8)&255)/255,b:(n&255)/255},opacity:o};};\nconst C={brand:\"#53B175\",dark:\"#181725\",gray:\"#7C7C7C\",light:\"#B1B1B1\",border:\"#E2E2E2\",surface:\"#F2F3F2\",white:\"#FFFFFF\",orange:\"#F3603F\"};\nconst MASTER={};for(const c of figma.root.findAllWithCriteria({types:[\"COMPONENT\"]}))MASTER[c.name]=c;\nconst SH=(y,r,a)=>[{type:\"DROP_SHADOW\",color:{r:0,g:0,b:0,a},offset:{x:0,y},radius:r,visible:true,blendMode:\"NORMAL\"}];\nfunction txt(ch,sz,st,col,w){const t=figma.createText();t.fontName={family:\"Poppins\",style:st};t.characters=ch;t.fontSize=sz;t.fills=[F(col)];if(w){t.textAutoResize=\"HEIGHT\";t.resize(w,t.height);}return t;}\nfunction svgI(d,size,color,filled){const s=`<svg width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\">`+(filled?`<path d=\"${d}\" fill=\"${color}\"/>`:`<path d=\"${d}\" stroke=\"${color}\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/>`)+`</svg>`;const n=figma.createNodeWithSvg(s);n.rescale(size/24);n.name=\"Icon\";return n;}\nfunction recolor(n,hex){const c=[F(hex)];const walk=l=>{if([\"VECTOR\",\"ELLIPSE\",\"RECTANGLE\",\"BOOLEAN_OPERATION\",\"LINE\",\"STAR\"].includes(l.type)){try{if(l.fills&&l.fills.length&&l.fills[0].visible!==false)l.fills=c;}catch(e){}try{if(l.strokes&&l.strokes.length&&l.strokes[0].visible!==false)l.strokes=c;}catch(e){}}if(l.type===\"TEXT\")l.fills=c;if(\"children\"in l)for(const ch of l.children)walk(ch);};walk(n);}\nfunction mediaInst(name,parent,x,y){const m=MASTER[name].createInstance();parent.appendChild(m);if(x!==undefined){m.x=x;m.y=y;}return m;}\nfunction fitIn(m,maxW,maxH){const s=Math.min(maxW/m.width,maxH/m.height);m.resize(m.width*s,m.height*s);}\n```\n\nWait, for components I need to use figma.createComponent() and then optionally convertToComponent. Let me build each:\n\n**Add Button**: 36×36, radius 12, brand fill, white plus icon centered.\n```js\nfunction mkComp(name,w,h){const c=figma.createComponent();c.resize(w,h);c.name=name;c.x=2250;c.y=compY;compY+=h+40;WS.appendChild(c);return c;}\nlet compY=0;\n```\n\nActually components need positions in the workspace page. Let me set x=2250 and stack vertically with spacing.\n\nAdd Button:\n```js\nconst ab=mkComp(\"Add Button\",36,36);\nab.cornerRadius=12;ab.fills=[F(C.brand)];ab.layoutMode=\"HORIZONTAL\";ab.primaryAxisAlignItems=\"CENTER\";ab.counterAxisAlignItems=\"CENTER\";\nconst plus=svgI(\"M12 5v14M5 12h14\",16,\"#FFFFFF\");plus.fills=[];ab.appendChild(plus);\n```\n\nWait — for auto-layout component, resizing: after setting layoutMode, the size changes. Better: set layoutMode first, then primaryAxisSizingMode=\"FIXED\", counterAxisSizingMode=\"FIXED\", then resize. Actually simpler: don't use auto-layout, just position the plus icon absolutely centered:\n```js\nconst ab=mkComp(\"Add Button\",36,36);ab.cornerRadius=12;ab.fills=[F(C.brand)];\nconst plus=svgI(\"M12 5v14M5 12h14\",16,\"#FFFFFF\");ab.appendChild(plus);plus.x=(36-plus.width)/2;plus.y=(36-plus.height)/2;\n```\n\nNote svgI with stroke — the SVG node will have a frame with fills? createNodeWithSvg returns a FrameNode containing vectors. The frame has fills=[] typically. When appending to a component, position it. But recolor on white icons — the svg is already white, fine.\n\nActually, the plus icon at 16px: the path \"M12 5v14M5 12h14\" in 24 viewBox with stroke-width 2. Rescaled to 16/24 = 0.667, stroke becomes ~1.33. Fine.\n\n**Quantity Stepper**: auto-layout H, gap 12? Actually original design has minus and plus circles with qty between. Let me do absolute positioning for simplicity: total width = 36+36+... Actually auto-layout is cleaner:\n\n```js\nconst qs=mkComp(\"Quantity Stepper\",115,36);\nqs.layoutMode=\"HORIZONTAL\";qs.primaryAxisSizingMode=\"AUTO\";qs.counterAxisSizingMode=\"AUTO\";qs.itemSpacing=14;qs.counterAxisAlignItems=\"CENTER\";qs.fills=[];\nconst minus=figma.createEllipse()... \n```\n\nHmm, minus button: 36×36 circle white fill, stroke #B1B1B1, with gray minus svg. I'll create a frame:\n```js\nfunction circBtn(d,color,bg,stroke){const f=figma.createFrame();f.resize(36,36);f.cornerRadius=18;f.fills=bg?[F(bg)]:[];if(stroke){f.strokes=[F(stroke)];f.strokeWeight=1;}const ic=svgI(d,16,color);f.appendChild(ic);ic.x=(36-ic.width)/2;ic.y=(36-ic.height)/2;return f;}\n```\n\nThen qty text \"1\" 16 SemiBold dark, name \"Qty\".\n\nFor the stepper as component: children minus frame, qty text, plus frame with auto-layout gap 14. Width = 36+14+~12+14+36 ≈ 112.\n\n**Product Card**: width 171, auto-layout V padding 12 gap 4? Let me compute: padding 12, image 147×86, name 16 Medium (~24 line), unit 14 (~21), price row ~36. Total ≈ 12+86+4+24+4+21+4+36+12 ≈ 203. \n\nActually simpler to build with absolute positioning inside fixed 171×~205 frame? Auto-layout is more robust. Let me do auto-layout:\n\n```js\nconst pc=mkComp(\"Product Card\",171,205);\npc.layoutMode=\"VERTICAL\";pc.primaryAxisSizingMode=\"AUTO\";pc.counterAxisSizingMode=\"FIXED\";pc.resize(171,100);pc.paddingLeft=pc.paddingRight=12;pc.paddingTop=pc.paddingBottom=12;pc.itemSpacing=6;pc.cornerRadius=18;pc.fills=[F(C.white)];pc.strokes=[F(C.border)];pc.strokeWeight=1;pc.effects=SH(4,16,0.06);\n```\n\nHmm, with counterAxisSizingMode FIXED and resize — order: set layoutMode, then resize(171, pc.height). Let me be careful: after layoutMode=\"VERTICAL\", width becomes hug of children. I'll set counterAxisSizingMode=\"FIXED\" then pc.resize(171,pc.height).\n\nImage frame:\n```js\nconst img=figma.createFrame();img.name=\"Image\";img.resize(147,86);img.fills=[];img.clipsContent=false;\nconst ph=mediaInst(\"Product_Red_Apple\",img);ph.name=\"Photo\";fitIn(ph,130,80);ph.x=(147-ph.width)/2;ph.y=(86-ph.height)/2;\npc.appendChild(img);\n```\n\nWait but in auto-layout, the image frame width should be 147 = 171-24. Good.\n\nName text: `const nm=txt(\"Red Apple\",16,\"Medium\",C.dark,147);` — with textAutoResize HEIGHT and width 147. In auto-layout V with counterAxis FIXED... child width 147 vs available 147. OK.\n\nActually with paddings 12+12=24, inner width = 171-24 = 147. Children at width 147 fill fully. Good.\n\nPrice row:\n```js\nconst row=figma.createFrame();row.name=\"Price Row\";row.fills=[];row.layoutMode=\"HORIZONTAL\";row.primaryAxisSizingMode=\"FIXED\";row.counterAxisSizingMode=\"AUTO\";row.resize(147,36);row.primaryAxisAlignItems=\"SPACE_BETWEEN\";row.counterAxisAlignItems=\"CENTER\";\nconst pr=txt(\"$4.99\",16,\"SemiBold\",C.dark);row.appendChild(pr);\nconst abInst=ab.createInstance();row.appendChild(abInst);\npc.appendChild(row);\n```\n\nHmm wait — ab is the Add Button component created earlier; I can create instances of components I just made. Yes.\n\n**Search Bar**: 366×49 radius 15 surface fill. Icon_Search instance recolored dark at (16,12.5); text at (52,15).\nWait Icon_Search dimensions — I don't recall exact; it was 24×24-ish. MASTER[\"Icon_Search\"].createInstance(), recolor to dark, then position. Let me scale to 20 if needed. I'll just use as-is centered at y.\n\nActually, from the summary: Icon_Search `4:160` — no dims listed. I'll use fitIn to 24 max and center.\n\n**Section Header**: auto-layout H SPACE_BETWEEN, width 366: Title 20 SemiBold dark + \"See all\" 16 Medium brand.\n\n```js\nconst sh=mkComp(\"Section Header\",366,30);\nsh.layoutMode=\"HORIZONTAL\";sh.primaryAxisSizingMode=\"FIXED\";sh.counterAxisSizingMode=\"AUTO\";sh.resize(366,30);sh.primaryAxisAlignItems=\"SPACE_BETWEEN\";sh.counterAxisAlignItems=\"CENTER\";sh.fills=[];\nconst st=txt(\"Title\",20,\"SemiBold\",C.dark);st.name=\"Title\";sh.appendChild(st);\nconst sa=txt(\"See all\",16,\"Medium\",C.brand);sa.name=\"SeeAll\";sh.appendChild(sa);\n```\n\n**Category Card**: 171×189 radius 18, tint fill (default #EAF6E9), Photo instance fit 120×112 at y14 centered, Label 15 Medium dark centered w171 at y146.\n\n```js\nconst cc=mkComp(\"Category Card\",171,189);cc.cornerRadius=18;cc.fills=[F(\"#EAF6E9\")];\nconst ph=mediaInst(\"Category_Fresh_Fruits_Vegetable\",cc);ph.name=\"Photo\";fitIn(ph,120,112);ph.x=(171-ph.width)/2;ph.y=14;\nconst lb=txt(\"Label\",15,\"Medium\",C.dark,171);lb.name=\"Label\";lb.textAlignHorizontal=\"CENTER\";lb.x=0;lb.y=146;\n```\n\n**Category Chip**: 171×64 radius 12 tint; Photo fit 40×40 at (12,12); Label 14 Medium dark at (62,22) w100.\n\nNow component y positions: compY starts 0, each mkComp places at x=2250, y=compY, then compY+=h+60.\n\nI need to also name instances properly so I can override them later (e.g., Photo name for swapComponent, Label name for text override, Qty name, Title name).\n\nImportant: for swapping photos in product card instances, I need to find the \"Photo\" instance inside the instance: `inst.findOne(n=>n.name===\"Photo\")` then swapComponent.\n\nAlso for overriding label text: find child by name and set characters (need font loaded — Poppins loaded).\n\nOK let me also think about whether `figma.root.findAllWithCriteria` includes components inside component sets (variants). MASTER map built from all COMPONENT nodes — varia