t after setting modes — before children appended. Then children appended; width stays 171 fixed. Height hugs. \n\nHmm, actually resize(171, pc.height): pc.height at that time ~24 (padding). That's fine.\n\nSimilarly for Button Secondary: layoutMode H, both FIXED, resize(364,67) after setting alignment. Children appended after — but with primaryAxisAlignItems=\"CENTER\" the label centers. Good.\n\nFor Section Header: layoutMode H, primaryAxisSizingMode=\"FIXED\", counterAxisSizingMode=\"AUTO\", resize(366,30) — then children; counterAxis AUTO → height hugs to tallest child (~30 for 20px text). SPACE_BETWEEN pushes See all right. Good.\n\nFor Checkout Row — absolute positioning, no auto-layout. Good.\n\nFor Quantity Stepper — absolute. Good.\n\nNow, the Component Set \"Tab Bar\": after combineAsVariants, set.position — combineAsVariants(variants, WS) puts it in WS; I set set.x=2250, set.y=cy (compute). Variant components inside get arranged. But note: variants were created as loose components on the page first (figma.createComponent appends to current page by default? Actually createComponent appends to figma.currentPage). Hmm — createComponent() appends to current page automatically. I should appendChild to WS or just let combineAsVariants move them. To be safe: after createComponent, don't worry; combineAsVariants moves them into the set. But before combining they'd sit on currentPage (which is whatever page is open — maybe 00 Start Here). They'd be moved into the set upon combine, so transient. OK.\n\nBut mk() for other components: figma.createComponent() appends to currentPage — I then WS.appendChild(c). Good.\n\nActually wait — does createComponent add to currentPage? Yes, like createFrame. And WS.appendChild moves it. Good.\n\nFor the variants loop, I won't append to WS; combineAsVariants handles.\n\nOne more: combineAsVariants signature: figma.combineAsVariants(nodes, parent, index). Good.\n\nAlso after combine, set.name=\"Tab Bar\".\n\nInstantiate tab bar later: MASTER[\"Tab Bar\"] will find the COMPONENT_SET — findAllWithCriteria types:[\"COMPONENT\"] won't include sets. For instantiation, I need a variant component: `set.children[0].createInstance()` then `inst.setProperties({ActiveTab:\"Explore\"})`. In later calls, MASTER rebuilt — I can find set via findOne: `figma.root.findOne(n=>n.type===\"COMPONENT_SET\"&&n.name===\"Tab Bar\")`. Then pick variant by name. Let me store: TB=figma.root.findOne(n=>n.type===\"COMPONENT_SET\"&&n.name===\"Tab Bar\"); then tbv(name)=TB.children.find(v=>v.name===\"ActiveTab=\"+name).\n\nAlright. Also for ids returned — I'll keep a mental note; but later calls can look up by name via findOne anyway. To be robust, later calls rebuild MASTER from findAllWithCriteria COMPONENT (includes my components and the variant components — variant names \"ActiveTab=Shop\" etc.). For \"Tab Bar\" set I use findOne by type COMPONENT_SET.\n\nLet me write Call 1a now. Also remember: return JSON.stringify at end.\n\nActually one more detail — the media icons like Icon_Search: are they instances or components with vector children? They're COMPONENT masters containing vectors. createInstance → instance. recolor walks instance children setting fills — allowed as override. Good.\n\nAlso Icon_Search may be white originally; recolor to dark #181725. Good.\n\nLet me also double-check `circ` helper used in both 1a (stepper) and maybe later (cart item uses stepper instance; verification uses Circle Button component + svg overlays at frame level). Fine.\n\nWrite Call 1a code. I'll aim for clean, compact code.\n\nCode (Call 1a):\n\n```js\nawait Promise.all([\"Regular\",\"Medium\",\"SemiBold\",\"Bold\"].map(s=>figma.loadFontAsync({family:\"Poppins\",style:s})));\nconst WS=figma.getNodeById(\"7:2\");\nconst F=(hex,o)=>{o=o===undefined?1:o;const n=parseInt(hex.slice(1),16);return{type:\"SOLID\",color:{r:((n>>16)&255)/255,g:((n>>8)&255)/255,b:(n&255)/255},opacity:o};};\nconst C={brand:\"#53B175\",dark:\"#181725\",gray:\"#7C7C7C\",light:\"#B1B1B1\",border:\"#E2E2E2\",surface:\"#F2F3F2\",white:\"#FFFFFF\"};\nconst MASTER={};for(const c of figma.root.findAllWithCriteria({types:[\"COMPONENT\"]}))MASTER[c.name]=c;\nconst SH=(y,r,a)=>[{type:\"DROP_SHADOW\",color:{r:0,g:0,b:0,a:a},offset:{x:0,y:y},radius:r,visible:true,blendMode:\"NORMAL\"}];\nfunction txt(ch,sz,st,col,w){const t=figma.createText();t.fontName={family:\"Poppins\",style:st};t.characters=ch;t.fontSize=sz;t.fills=[F(col)];if(w){t.textAutoResize=\"HEIGHT\";t.resize(w,t.height);}return t;}\nfunction svgI(d,size,color){const s='<svg width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><path d=\"'+d+'\" stroke=\"'+color+'\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/></svg>';const n=figma.createNodeWithSvg(s);n.rescale(size/24);n.name=\"Icon\";n.fills=[];return n;}\nfunction mediaInst(name,parent){const m=MASTER[name].createInstance();parent.appendChild(m);return m;}\nfunction fitIn(m,w,h){const s=Math.min(w/m.width,h/m.height);m.resize(m.width*s,m.height*s);}\nlet cy=0;for(const ch of WS.children)cy=Math.max(cy,ch.y+ch.height+60);\nconst ids={};\nfunction mk(name,w,h){const c=figma.createComponent();WS.appendChild(c);c.x=2250;c.y=cy;cy+=h+60;c.resizeWithoutConstraints(w,h);c.name=name;ids[name]=c.id;return c;}\nconst ab=mk(\"Add Button\",36,36);ab.cornerRadius=12;ab.fills=[F(C.brand)];\nconst pi=svgI(\"M12 5v14M5 12h14\",16,\"#FFFFFF\");ab.appendChild(pi);pi.x=(36-pi.width)/2;pi.y=(36-pi.height)/2;\nfunction circ(icCol,bg,stroke){const f=figma.createFrame();f.resize(36,36);f.cornerRadius=18;f.fills=bg?[F(bg)]:[];if(stroke){f.strokes=[F(stroke)];f.strokeWeight=1;}return f;}\nconst qs=mk(\"Quantity Stepper\",114,36);qs.fills=[];\nconst mb=circ(C.gray,C.white,C.light);mb.name=\"Minus\";const mi=svgI(\"M5 12h14\",16,C.gray);mb.appendChild(mi);mi.x=(36-mi.width)/2;mi.y=(36-mi.height)/2;qs.appendChild(mb);mb.x=0;mb.y=0;\nconst qt=txt(\"1\",16,\"SemiBold\",C.dark);qt.name=\"Qty\";qs.appendChild(qt);qt.x=50;qt.y=(36-qt.height)/2;\nconst pb=circ(\"#FFFFFF\",C.brand,null);pb.name=\"Plus\";const pi2=svgI(\"M12 5v14M5 12h14\",16,\"#FFFFFF\");pb.appendChild(pi2);pi2.x=(36-pi2.width)/2;pi2.y=(36-pi2.height)/2;qs.appendChild(pb);pb.x=78;pb.y=0;\nconst pc=mk(\"Product Card\",171,206);pc.layoutMode=\"VERTICAL\";pc.counterAxisSizingMode=\"FIXED\";pc.primaryAxisSizingMode=\"AUTO\";pc.paddingLeft=12;pc.paddingRight=12;pc.paddingTop=12;pc.paddingBottom=12;pc.itemSpacing=6;pc.cornerRadius=18;pc.fills=[F(C.white)];pc.strokes=[F(C.border)];pc.effects=SH(4,16,0.06);pc.resize(171,206);\nconst img=figma.createFrame();img.name=\"Image\";img.resize(147,86);img.fills=[];pc.appendChild(img);\nconst ph=mediaInst(\"Product_Red_Apple\",img);ph.name=\"Photo\";fitIn(ph,130,80);ph.x=(147-ph.width)/2;ph.y=(86-ph.height)/2;\nconst nm=txt(\"Red Apple\",16,\"Medium\",C.dark,147);nm.name=\"Name\";pc.appendChild(nm);\nconst un=txt(\"1kg, Price\",14,\"Regular\",C.gray,147);un.name=\"Unit\";pc.appendChild(un);\nconst row=figma.createFrame();row.name=\"PriceRow\";row.fills=[];row.layoutMode=\"HORIZONTAL\";row.primaryAxisSizingMode=\"FIXED\";row.counterAxisSizingMode=\"AUTO\";row.primaryAxisAlignItems=\"SPACE_BETWEEN\";row.counterAxisAlignItems=\"CENTER\";row.resize(147,36);\nconst pr=txt(\"$4.99\",16,\"SemiBold\",C.dark);pr.name=\"Price\";row.appendChild(pr);\nconst ai=ab.createInstance();row.appendChild(ai);\npc.appendChild(row);\nconst sb=mk(\"Search Bar\",366,49);sb.cornerRadius=15;sb.fills=[F(C.surface)];\nconst si=mediaInst(\"Icon_Search\",sb);si.name=\"SearchIcon\";recolor... \n```\n\nOops — I removed recolor from this draft. I need recolor helper! Add:\n\n```js\nfunction recolor(n,hex){const c=[F(hex)];const walk=l=>{if([\"VECTOR\",\"ELLIPSE\",\"RECTANGLE\",\"BOOLEAN_OPERATION\",\"LINE\",\"STAR\"].indexOf(l.type)>=0){try{if(l.fills&&l.fills.length&&l.fills[0].visible!==false)l.fills=c;}catch(e){}try{if(l.strokes&&l.strokes.length&&l.strokes[0].visible!==false)l.strokes=c;}catch(e){}}if(l.type===\"TEXT\")l.fills=c;if(\"children\"in l){for(const ch2 of l.children)walk(ch2);}};walk(n);}\n```\n\nContinue Search Bar:\n```js\nrecolor(si,C.dark);fitIn(si,24,24);si.x=16;si.y=(49-si.height)/2;\nconst sp=txt(\"Search Store\",14,\"Regular\",C.gray);sp.name=\"Placeholder\";sb.appendChild(sp);sp.x=52;sp.y=(49-sp.height)/2;\nconst shdr=mk(\"Section Header\",366,30);shdr.layoutMode=\"HORIZONTAL\";shdr.primaryAxisSizingMode=\"FIXED\";shdr.counterAxisSizingMode=\"AUTO\";shdr.primaryAxisAlignItems=\"SPACE_BETWEEN\";shdr.counterAxisAlignItems=\"CENTER\";shdr.fills=[];shdr.resize(366,30);\nconst h1=txt(\"Title\",20,\"SemiBold\",C.dark);h1.name=\"Title\";shdr.appendChild(h1);\nconst sa2=txt(\"See all\",16,\"Medium\",C.brand);sa2.name=\"SeeAll\";shdr.appendChild(sa2);\nconst cc=mk(\"Category Card\",171,189);cc.cornerRadius=18;cc.fills=[F(\"#EAF6E9\")];cc.clipsContent=true;\nconst cp=mediaInst(\"Category_Fresh_Fruits_Vegetable\",cc);cp.name=\"Photo\";fitIn(cp,120,112);cp.x=(171-cp.width)/2;cp.y=14;\nconst cl=txt(\"Label\",15,\"Medium\",C.dark,171);cl.name=\"Label\";cl.textAlignHorizontal=\"CENTER\";cl.x=0;cl.y=146;\nconst chip=mk(\"Category Chip\",171,64);chip.cornerRadius=12;chip.fills=[F(\"#EAF6E9\")];chip.clipsContent=true;\nconst hp=mediaInst(\"Category_Rice\",chip);hp.name=\"Photo\";fitIn(hp,40,40);hp.x=12;hp.y=12;\nconst hl2=txt(\"Label\",14,\"Medium\",C.dark,100);hl2.name=\"Label\";hl2.x=62;hl2.y=(64-hl2.height)/2;\nreturn JSON.stringify({ids:ids,cy:cy});\n```\n\nCount: ~4.9k chars. \n\nOne concern: `pc.resize(171,206)` after setting primaryAxisSizingMode=\"AUTO\" — resizing to 206 sets fixed? With AUTO, after appendChild the height re-hugs. The resize is harmless. Actually there's a subtlety: resize() on auto-layout sets the size but AUTO axis re-hugs on next layout. Fine.\n\nAlso img frame: clipsContent default true for createFrame; I want false so photo can overflow? I sized photo to fit within 147×86, so clipping irrelevant. Leave