{"type":"assistant","message":{"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"`figma.createNodeWithSvg` is not available in this environment. I need another way to create icons. Options:\n\n1. Use `figma.createVector()` and set vectorPaths — this is a real API: `node.vectorPaths = [{windingRule:\"NONZERO\", data:\"M ...\"}]`. vectorPaths data uses SVG-ish path syntax but limited (M, L, Q, C, Z with absolute coords). Actually vectorPaths supports \"M L Q C Z\" commands with absolute coordinates. Stroke-based icons: I can create vector with path data and set strokes, strokeWeight, strokeCap ROUND, strokeJoin ROUND, fills=[].\n\n2. Use figma.createLine / createEllipse / createRectangle for simple shapes.\n\n3. Use the existing media icons via instances + recolor (chevrons etc. — Icon_Chevron_Right exists as media component! I can instance it, recolor, and rotate/mirror for chevron-left/down).\n\nGiven createNodeWithSvg is unavailable, I'll build a vector-based icon helper:\n\n```js\nfunction vec(d,size,color,strokeW){const v=figma.createVector();v.vectorPaths=[{windingRule:\"NONE\",data:d}];v.strokes=[F(color)];v.strokeWeight=strokeW||2;v.strokeCap=\"ROUND\";v.strokeJoin=\"ROUND\";v.fills=[];v.resize?...}\n```\n\nHmm — setting vectorPaths: the vector auto-sizes to path bounds? Actually when you set vectorPaths, the node's size adjusts to the path's bounding box... I believe the vector keeps size 100×100 default and paths render; then handleGeometry... Let me recall: `vectorPaths` setter — \"Setting this property will resize the node to fit its contents\"? I think the vector node's width/height update to the bounding box of the path data. Yes, setting vectorPaths rescales the node coordinates — the node bounds become the path bounds.\n\nImportant: path data in vectorPaths must use only M, L, Q, C, Z (no arcs A, no lowercase relative commands? Actually relative lowercase is allowed? The docs: \"data\" supports a subset of SVG path syntax: M, L, Q, C, Z (both cases?). To be safe use only absolute M/L/C/Q/Z.\n\nMy icon paths use only M, L, and implicit lines with l (relative). E.g. \"M6 9l6 6 6-6\" uses lowercase l. I should convert to absolute L commands. Also rounded-rect arcs \"a2 2 0 0 0...\" are NOT supported — must avoid arcs.\n\nLet me redefine icons with absolute coordinates, no arcs:\n\n- plus: \"M12 5 L12 19 M5 12 L19 12\" → as one path with two subpaths. vectorPaths data can contain multiple subpaths in one string? I believe yes, space-separated commands. Multiple M commands allowed.\n- minus: \"M5 12 L19 12\"\n- chevron-down: \"M6 9 L12 15 L18 9\"\n- chevron-left: \"M15 5 L8 12 L15 19\"\n- chevron-right: \"M9 5 L16 12 L9 19\"\n- close: \"M6 6 L18 18 M18 6 L6 18\"\n- filter: \"M4 7 L20 7 M7 12 L17 12 M10 17 L14 17\"\n- share: \"M12 3 L12 14 M8 6 L12 2.5 L16 6\" hmm arrow head: \"M8.5 6.5 L12 3 L15.5 6.5\" plus box \"M8 10 L6 10 L6 20 L18 20 L18 10 L16 10\". Use lines only.\n- pencil: \"M4 20 L8 19 L19 8 L16 5 L5 16 L4 20 Z\" — actually pencil outline fine as stroke path: \"M4 20 L5 16 L16 5 L19 8 L8 19 Z\"? Simplify: \"M14.5 4.5 L19.5 9.5 M4 20 L5 16 L15.5 5.5 L18.5 8.5 L8 19 L4 20 Z\". Multiple subpaths OK.\n- logout: \"M9 21 L5 21 C3.9 21 3 20.1 3 19 L3 5 C3 3.9 3.9 3 5 3 L9 3 M16 17 L21 12 L16 7 M21 12 L9 12\" — C curves allowed. Or use lines: \"M9 21 L5 21 L5 3 L9 3 M16 17 L21 12 L16 7 M21 12 L9 12\". Simpler with lines.\n- star filled: needs fill not stroke. For filled star: vectorPaths with windingRule NONZERO and fills=[F(color)], strokes=[]. Star path absolute: \"M12 2 L14.9 8.2 L21.5 9 L16.6 13.6 L17.9 20.1 L12 16.9 L6.1 20.1 L7.4 13.6 L2.5 9 L9.1 8.2 L12 2 Z\".\n\nAlso for the filled version, my svgF helper: create vector, fills, no strokes.\n\nFor vector sizing: after setting vectorPaths, node bounds = path bounds (e.g., plus spans 5..19 → 14×14). Then I position by centering within parent: x=(parent.width-v.width)/2. That works since bounds are tight. For stroke weight 2, strokes extend beyond bounds by 1px — fine visually.\n\nActually careful: with strokeCap ROUND and strokeWeight 2, endpoints extend 1px. Fine.\n\nBut wait — does setting vectorPaths adjust node width/height? From Figma docs: \"vectorPaths: VectorPaths[] — Applicable only on nodes with vectorChildren... setting this will normalize...\" Hmm. Actually VectorNode.vectorPaths — when set, the node resizes to fit the paths. I believe the behavior: the vector network is set in the node's local coordinates, and the node's size becomes the bounding box of the geometry. Let me just test empirically in the code: after setting vectorPaths, log width/height. I'll include a normalization: v.x/v.y set relative to computed bounds.\n\nAlternative safer approach: wrap each icon vector in a frame of known size and center the vector by its reported width/height after setting paths (read v.width/v.height at runtime and center). That works regardless.\n\nLet me redefine svgI as:\n\n```js\nfunction icn(d,size,color,filled){const v=figma.createVector();if(filled){v.vectorPaths=[{windingRule:\"NONZERO\",data:d}];v.fills=[F(color)];v.strokes=[];}else{v.vectorPaths=[{windingRule:\"NONE\",data:d}];v.strokes=[F(color)];v.strokeWeight=2;v.strokeCap=\"ROUND\";v.strokeJoin=\"ROUND\";v.fills=[];}v.name=\"Icon\";const s=size/Math.max(v.width,v.height);v.rescale(s);return v;}\n```\n\nHmm — rescale exists on most nodes. VectorNode.rescale? rescale is a method on LayoutMixin? Actually `rescale` is available on many nodes (it's `rescale(scale: number): void` on LayoutMixin? I recall node.rescale exists for most scene nodes). Previously I used n.rescale(size/24) on the SVG frame — untested too. Risk. Alternative: v.resize(v.width*s, v.height*s) — but that scales geometry? resize on vector scales the vector network? For VectorNode, resize scales the paths? I believe resize stretches the vector network to the new size (yes, vector geometry scales with resize since it has no constraints... actually vectors scale their geometry on resize). Hmm, not 100% sure: For a VectorNode, resize changes width/height and the vector data stretches. I think yes — vector children scale with resize.\n\nSimpler robust approach: since I design paths in a 24×24 coordinate space, I can keep vectors at natural bounds and just accept their size, OR author the paths at the final pixel size directly! E.g., for a 16px plus icon, author \"M8 1 L8 15 M1 8 L15 8\" in 16-space. That avoids all scaling issues.\n\nLet me define icons per-use at required sizes:\n\nSizes needed:\n- plus white 16 (Add Button, Plus circle): path in 16-box: \"M8 2 L8 14 M2 8 L14 8\" — bounds 12×12 (2..14).\n- minus gray 16: \"M2 8 L14 8\"\n- chevron icons: various 12-20.\n- close/remove 14: \"M2 2 L12 12 M12 2 L2 12\" (14-box).\n- star 16 filled: author star in 16-box.\n\nSince authoring at exact sizes is error-prone, better: author in 24-space, then use v.resize(targetW, targetH)? Bounds differ per icon (plus spans 14 of 24). \n\nCleanest: helper that takes path in 24-box, desired *bound* size = size*(bound/24) where bound is the 24-space extent. Overcomplicating.\n\nPragmatic approach: create vector, read v.width/v.height (bounds of geometry in 24-space), then v.resize(v.width*k, v.height*k) with k=size/24. If resize scales geometry — good. If resize does NOT scale vector geometry (just crops), the icon would be clipped... Risk.\n\nLet me check knowledge: Figma Plugin API VectorNode — \"resize(width, height): Resizes the node. For vectors, the vector network is scaled to fit.\" I'm fairly confident vector geometry scales on resize (like scaling a shape in the UI). Yes — resizing a vector layer in Figma UI scales its geometry; the API resize does the same for vectors (they have no children constraints).\n\nHmm, actually there's nuance: resize vs resizeWithoutConstraints. For VectorNode both scale geometry. I'll go with resize scaling, and verify via screenshot later.\n\nEven safer: use vNetwork? No. Keep it simple; verify visually.\n\nAlternative approach that avoi