 Good look.\n\nFor filled star: fills scale with geometry fine.\n\nNow rewrite Call 1a with vector icons:\n\n```js\nfunction icn(d,size,color,filled){const v=figma.createVector();v.vectorPaths=[{windingRule:filled?\"NONZERO\":\"NONE\",data:d}];if(filled){v.fills=[F(color)];v.strokes=[];}else{v.strokes=[F(color)];v.strokeWeight=2;v.strokeCap=\"ROUND\";v.strokeJoin=\"ROUND\";v.fills=[];}v.name=\"Icon\";const k=size/24;v.resize(v.width*k,v.height*k);return v;}\n```\n\nIcon paths (24-box, absolute, no arcs):\n- PLUS: \"M12 5 L12 19 M5 12 L19 12\"\n- MINUS: \"M5 12 L19 12\"\n- CLOSE: \"M6 6 L18 18 M18 6 L6 18\"\n\nAdd Button: icn(PLUS,16,\"#FFFFFF\") → width=(19-5)*2/3≈9.3? wait k=16/24=0.667, bounds 14×14 → 9.3×9.3. Hmm that's smaller than intended 16 (because bound is 14 not 24). The icon will look small-ish in 36 button. I want the drawn size ~16px. So pass size relative: desired drawn extent 16 → k=16/14≈1.143. Ugh, per-icon bounds vary.\n\nFix: helper computes k = size/24 assuming \"size\" is full 24-space scale. For plus at 16 → drawn 9.3px — too small. Better: I'll pass desired size as the *geometry extent* multiplier: helper param `s` = scale factor applied to geometry extent: v.resize(v.width*s, v.height*s) where s chosen per icon so drawn size matches target. Simplest: helper takes target drawn size for the LARGER dimension:\n\n```js\nfunction icn(d,t,color,filled){const v=figma.createVector();...;const m=Math.max(v.width,v.height);const k=t/m;v.resize(v.width*k,v.height*k);return v;}\n```\nSo icn(PLUS,16,\"#FFFFFF\") → plus becomes 16×16 drawn. chevron-down \"M6 9 L12 15 L18 9\" bounds 12×6; target 14 → k=14/12 → 14×7 drawn. Good — t = desired max dimension.\n\nCentering: parent centers by v.width/v.height measured — fine.\n\nNow update all uses:\n- Add Button: plus 16 white.\n- Minus: minus 14 gray (#7C7C7C). Plus: plus 14 white? Slightly smaller than 16 looks fine. Use 14 both.\n- Stepper qty.\n\nOK. Also chevron paths:\n- CHD (down): \"M6 9 L12 15 L18 9\"\n- CHL (left): \"M15 5 L8 12 L15 19\" bounds 7×14\n- CHR (right): \"M9 5 L16 12 L9 19\"\n- CLOSE: \"M5 5 L19 19 M19 5 L5 19\" bounds 14×14\n- FILTER: \"M4 7 L20 7 M7 12 L17 12 M10 17 L14 17\" bounds 16×10\n- SHARE: \"M12 3 L12 14 M8.5 6 L12 2.5 L15.5 6 M8 10 L6 10 L6 20 L18 20 L18 10 L16 10\" bounds ~12.5×17.5. t=20.\n- PENCIL: \"M4 20 L5 16 L15.5 5.5 L18.5 8.5 L8 19 L4 20 Z\" bounds 14.5×14.5. t=16.\n- LOGOUT: \"M9 21 L5 21 L5 3 L9 3 M16 17 L21 12 L16 7 M21 12 L9 12\" bounds 16×18. t=20.\n- STAR filled: \"M12 2 L14.9 8.2 L21.5 9 L16.6 13.6 L17.9 20.1 L12 16.9 L6.1 20.1 L7.4 13.6 L2.5 9 L9.1 8.2 L12 2 Z\" t=16, color #F3603F.\n\nAlso \"circ\" helper for stepper circles.\n\nAlso — one more thing: vectorPaths setter may throw if data has unsupported commands; my paths use only M/L/Z — safe.\n\nAlso note: in the previous call, \"Add Button\" component etc. were NOT created (error at svgI before... actually error occurred at line creating pi in Add Button — after mk(\"Add Button\") and ab created; the component \"Add Button\" exists empty! The call failed mid-way, so partial state: \"Add Button\" component (empty, 36×36) created at 2250,0; then error. Everything after didn't run. So workspace has a stray empty \"Add Button\" component. I should delete it at the start of the retry: remove empty components or reuse. Simplest: at start, delete ALL children of WS? Nothing else exists there (page was empty before; only the stray Add Button). Deleting the stray component I just created is safe — it's my own scratch. Do: `for(const ch of [...WS.children])ch.remove();` then rebuild fresh. That keeps clean state. But careful: if the retry partially fails again, same cleanup next time. OK.\n\nAlso remove `n.fills=[]` on frame — vectors now.\n\nRewrite Call 1a fully with icn() and cleanup.","signature":"04ee814d8d7c418587beb8b6"}],"id":"76a7222d-48e2-44e1-b2c9-0206e03a1355","model":"glm-5.3-flash","role":"assistant","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{