{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\n<tools-used-before-summary>mcp__figma__get_metadata, mcp__figma__use_figma, mcp__figma__whoami</tools-used-before-summary>\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   Complete an unattended Figma product design benchmark. Assigned file: https://www.figma.com/design/aBJm2MvkIZqCV7cu0O7PHX/ (fileKey `aBJm2MvkIZqCV7cu0O7PHX`). Original user request (Chinese): Read the design task in「00·Start Here」, follow visual specs in「01·Foundations」, reuse components from「02·Components」, use assets from「04·Media」, and deliver the complete design to「03·Workspace」.\n\n   Binding constraints (system/task instructions):\n   - whoami was called earlier; account confirmed as huangxinyue@tetras.ai (handle \"huangxinyue\").\n   - Use ONLY this assigned file; preserve all reference pages (0:1, 1:2, 1:3, 1:4) and their nodes; do not create a different file or switch accounts/teams.\n   - Create everything inside 03 · Workspace (page `7:2`); new frames, reusable components and prototype connections allowed there.\n   - Before EVERY tool call include a concise visible decision summary prefixed exactly `Reasoning summary:` in the same assistant message; after each tool result do the same. Final response: first line `Reasoning summary: ...`, then `Final answer:` with the assigned file URL, the 03 · Workspace page ID, screen IDs, prototype work completed, and remaining limitations. Never claim completion for unfinished work.\n   - Load fonts before editing text; valid Plugin API only; NEVER use loadAllPagesAsync, setPluginData, createImageAsync.\n   - Build in manageable sections; verify with get_screenshot; finish screens + states + prototype flows before final answer. Unattended session — resolve routine choices from the brief without waiting.\n\n   Product brief (from 00 · Start Here, binding): \"Nectar\" online groceries app, canvas 414×896, light mode, exactly 12 frames with exact names, wired as a clickable prototype. Fixed data/copy (verbatim, brief wins over source-kit typos):\n   - Shopper: Afsar Hossen · imshuvo97@gmail.com · avatar = Avatar_Neutral · Location: Dhaka, Banasree · phone +880 (Flag_Bangladesh) · unit format \"1kg, Price\"\n   - Catalog (name · size · price · image master): Organic Bananas · 7pcs · $4.99 · Product_Organic_Bananas; Red Apple · 1kg · $4.99 · Product_Red_Apple (detail title \"Natural Red Apple\"); Bell Pepper Red · 1kg · $4.99 · Product_Bell_Pepper_Red; Ginger · 250gm · $2.99 · Product_Ginger; Beef Bone · 1kg · $4.99 · Product_Beef_Bone; Broiler Chicken · 1kg · $4.99 · Product_Broiler_Chicken; Egg Chicken Red · 4pcs · $1.99 · Product_Egg_Chicken_Red\n   - Beverages: Diet Coke · 355ml · $1.99; Sprite Can · 325ml · $1.50; Apple & Grape Juice · 2L · $15.99; Orange Juice · 2L · $15.99; Coca Cola Can · 325ml · $4.99; Pepsi Can · 330ml · $4.99\n   - Home: \"Dhaka, Banasree\"; search \"Search Store\"; Promotion \"Fresh Vegetables\" / \"Get Up To 40% OFF\" (Banner_Fresh_Vegetables); Exclusive Offer: Organic Bananas, Red Apple; Best Selling: Bell Pepper Red, Ginger; Groceries: categories Pulses (Category_Pulses), Rice (Category_Rice); products Beef Bone, Broiler Chicken\n   - Product detail: \"Natural Red Apple\" · \"1kg, Price\" · qty 1 · $4.99; description exactly: \"Apples are nutritious. Apples may be good for weight loss. Apples may be good for your heart. As part of a healthful and varied diet.\"; Nutritions 100gr; Review 5 of 5 stars\n   - Cart/checkout: Bell Pepper Red $4.99 · Egg Chicken Red $1.99 · Organic Bananas $4.99 · Ginger $2.99, qty 1 each, Total $14.96 everywhere (use $14.96, NOT the source's wrong $12.96/$13.97); Delivery \"Select Method\" · Promo Code \"Pick discount\"; legal \"By placing an order you agree to our Terms And Conditions\"\n   - Explore: \"Find Products\"; search \"Search Store\"; 6 categories: Fresh Fruits & Vegetable, Cooking Oil & Ghee, Meat & Fish, Bakery & Snacks, Dairy & Eggs, Beverages (images Category_*)\n   - Sign in: \"Get your groceries with nectar\" · +880 · \"Or connect with social media\" · Continue with Google · Continue with Facebook; Verification: \"Enter your 4-digit code\" · \"Code\" · Resend Code (4 digits, none entered); Onboarding: \"Welcome to our store\" · \"Get your groceries in as fast as one hour\" · Get Started; Accepted: \"Your Order has been accepted\" · \"Your items have been placed and are on their way to being processed\" · Track Order · Back to home\n   - Account: Afsar Hossen · imshuvo97@gmail.com; entries Orders · My Details · Delivery Address · Payment Methods · Promo Code · Notifications · Help · About · Log Out\n\n   Navigation rules: Main nav (Tab Bar) on frames 05, 07, 09, 12 — five tabs in order Shop(Icon_Shop)→05, Explore(Icon_Explore)→07, Cart(Icon_Cart)→09, Favourite(Icon_Favourite, entry only, no link), Account(Icon_Account)→12; current tab must match frame. Pushed screens with back: 04 (→03 back), 06 (→05), 08 (→07); 06 & 08 have NO main nav. 10_Checkout_Overlay opens over 09 (cart visible behind); → Place Order → 11. Entry-only (NO links needed): See all, add to cart, share, favourite, filter, Resend Code, social sign-in buttons, Track Order, Favourite tab, Delivery/Payment/Promo rows, account entries, edit name, Log Out. NO extra frames beyond the 12. Frame links: 01_Splash auto(AFTER_DELAY ~2000)→02; 02 Get Started→03; 03 phone field→04; 04 back→03, next→05; 05 Red Apple card→06, tabs; 06 back→05, Add To Basket→09; 07 Beverages card→08, tabs; 08 back→07; 09 Go to Checkout→10, tabs; 10 close→09, Place Order→11; 11 Back to home→05; 12 tabs. Flow start on 01_Splash.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Figma Plugin API via `mcp__figma__use_figma` (code ≤50000 chars; MUST `return JSON.stringify(...)` as last statement — console.log doesn't surface).\n   - **RESTRICTED ENVIRONMENT**: `figma.createNodeWithSvg` DOES NOT EXIST (\"no such property on the figma global object\") — custom icons must use `figma.createVector()` + `vectorPaths` (absolute M/L/Z commands only, no arcs).\n   - **Failed use_figma calls are TRANSACTIONAL** — all changes roll back (verified twice). Re-issue the whole call after fixing.\n   - `figma.createComponent()` appends to figma.currentPage; `figma.combineAsVariants(nodes, parent)` requires nodes already on the same page as parent → always `WS.appendChild(v)` after creating variant components.\n   - CURRENT UNRESOLVED BUG: `.findOne(...)` on an InstanceNode returned null in the frames call (both suspected sites: Text Field instance label override and/or Social Button Label override) even though masters have TEXT children. Fix in progress: replace ALL `.findOne` with manual recursion over `.children` (`findN`/`findTxt`/`findByName`) plus defensive `setChars` that records failures instead of throwing.\n   - `node.resize()` on vectors scales geometry but keeps strokeWeight (2px) — acceptable chunky look; `rescale()` avoided.\n   - `vectorPaths` setter: node bounds become path bounds; `icn()` helper scales so max dimension = target size.\n   - Component instantiation + nested-instance overrides: text characters override, `swapComponent()` for photo/icon swaps, `instance.fills` override, child `visible` toggles — all used successfully in component library calls.\n   - Intermittent MCP rate limits (\"You've reached the Figma MCP tool call limit...\") — retry the identical call; it usually succeeds.\n   - `figma.getNodeById` (NOT getPageById). Poppins Regular/Medium/SemiBold/Bold must be loaded per call before text work (Inter not used; \"Semi Bold\" spacing issue doesn't apply to Poppins — style is \"SemiBold\").\n   - Prototype reactions: `node.reactions=[{action:{type:\"NODE\",destinationId,navigation:\"NAVIGATE\",transition:null,overlay:null},trigger:{type:\"CLICK\"}}]`; AFTER_DELAY trigger `{type:\"AFTER_DELAY\",delay:2000}`; `frame.flowStartingPoint={nodeId,name}` wrapped in try/catch; transparent hotspot rects over tab-bar regions for nav links.\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - **Figma file aBJm2MvkIZqCV7cu0O7PHX** — pages: `0:1` (00 · Start Here), `1:2` (01 · Foundations), `1:3` (02 · Components), `1:4` (04 · Media), `7:2` (03 · Workspace — delivery target; currently contains ONLY the 16 created components, no frames yet). Reference pages untouched (verified extra ActiveTab orphans = 0 on all other pages).\n\n   - **CREATED workspace components (page 7:2), all verified present**:\n     - Add Button `11:2` (36×36, radius 12, #53B175, white plus vector)\n     - Quantity Stepper `11:4` (114×36: Minus circle white/stroke #B1B1B1 + gray minus; \"Qty\" text name=\"Qty\" \"1\" 16 SemiBold; Plus circle brand + white plus; children named Minus/Qty/Plus)\n     - Product Card `11:10` (171 wide auto-layout V, padding 12, gap 6, radius 18, white, stroke #E2E2E2, shadow SH(4,16,0.06); children: frame \"Image\" 147×86 containing instance \"Photo\" (default Product_Red_Apple fit 130×80 centered); \"Name\" 16 Medium w147; \"Unit\" 14 Regular gray w147; frame \"PriceRow\" (147 wide, SPACE_BETWEEN, center) containing \"Price\" 16 SemiBold + Add Button instance) — ~206 tall\n     - Search Bar `11:19` (366×49 radius 15 #F2F3F2; \"SearchIcon\" = Icon_Search instance recolored dark fit 24 at x16; \"Placeholder\" \"Search Store\" 14 Regular gray at x52)\n     - Section Header `11:23` (auto-layout H 366, SPACE_BETWEEN, center; \"Title\" 20 SemiBold dark + \"SeeAll\" \"See all\" 16 Medium brand)\n     - Category Card `11:26` (171×189 radius 18, default tint #EAF6E9, clipsContent; \"Photo\" instance fit 120×112 at y14 centered; \"Label\" 15 Medium dark centered w171 y146)\n     - Category Chip `11:29` (171×64 radius 12 tint #EAF6E9; \"Photo\" fit 40×40 at (12,12); \"Label\" 14 Medium dark w100 at (62, centered))\n     - Tab Bar COMPONENT_SET `11:370` — variants \"ActiveTab=Shop/Explore/Cart/Favourite/Account