×40 at y24 containing RECTANGLE \"Underline\" `6:38` 364×1 #E2E2E2); Status Bar `6:43` (414×44 white bg, black icons); Home Indicator `6:54` (414×34 white bg, black bar).\n\n   - **Media masters (04 · Media, all COMPONENT)**: Nectar_Carrot `4:10` (29×34), Nectar_Logo `4:13` (180×45), Nectar_Logo_White `4:16` (180×45); Product_Apple_Grape_Juice `4:22` (180×180), Product_Beef_Bone `4:25` (180×89), Product_Bell_Pepper_Red `4:28` (180×155), Product_Broiler_Chicken `4:31` (180×120), Product_Coca_Cola_Can `4:34` (97×180), Product_Diet_Coke `4:37` (90×180), Product_Egg_Chicken_Red `4:40` (180×180), Product_Ginger `4:43` (180×162), Product_Orange_Juice `4:46` (180×180), Product_Organic_Bananas `4:49` (180×144), Product_Pepsi_Can `4:52` (126×180), Product_Red_Apple `4:55` (180×109), Product_Sprite_Can `4:58` (108×180); Category_Bakery_Snacks `4:64` (180×180), Category_Beverages `4:67` (180×135), Category_Cooking_Oil_Ghee `4:70` (180×180), Category_Dairy_Eggs `4:73` (180×126), Category_Fresh_Fruits_Vegetable `4:76` (180×121), Category_Meat_Fish `4:79` (180×151), Category_Pulses `4:82` (180×180), Category_Rice `4:85` (177×180); Banner_Fresh_Vegetables `4:91` (180×145), Photo_Sign_In_Groceries `4:94` (180×120), Photo_Welcome_Delivery `4:97` (180×120); Avatar_Neutral `4:103` (128×128), Flag_Bangladesh `4:106` (180×108), Illustration_Order_Accepted `4:109` (180×158); Icons (white, recolor on light bg): Icon_About `4:115`, Icon_Account `4:118` (20×24), Icon_Cart `4:121` (24×22), Icon_Chevron_Right `4:124` (16×24), Icon_Delivery_Address `4:127` (20×24), Icon_Explore `4:130` (24×16), Icon_Facebook_White `4:133` (13×24), Icon_Favourite `4:136` (24×21), Icon_Google_White `4:139` (23×24), Icon_Help `4:142`, Icon_My_Details `4:145` (24×19), Icon_Notifications `4:148` (22×24), Icon_Orders `4:151` (22×24), Icon_Payment `4:154` (24×17), Icon_Promo `4:157`, Icon_Search `4:160`, Icon_Shop `4:163`.\n\n   - **WORKING helper code** (used verbatim at top of successful calls; reuse in all subsequent calls):\n     ```js\n     await Promise.all([\"Regular\",\"Medium\",\"SemiBold\",\"Bold\"].map(s=>figma.loadFontAsync({family:\"Poppins\",style:s})));\n     const WS=figma.getNodeById(\"7:2\");\n     const F=(hex,o)=>{o=o===undefined?1:o;const n=parseInt(hex.slice(1),16);return{type:\"SOLID\",color:{r:((n>>16)&255)/255,g:((n>>8)&255)/255,b:(n&255)/255},opacity:o};};\n     const C={brand:\"#53B175\",dark:\"#181725\",gray:\"#7C7C7C\",light:\"#B1B1B1\",border:\"#E2E2E2\",surface:\"#F2F3F2\",white:\"#FFFFFF\",orange:\"#F3603F\"};\n     const MASTER={};for(const c of figma.root.findAllWithCriteria({types:[\"COMPONENT\"]}))MASTER[c.name]=c;\n     const SH=(y,r,a)=>[{type:\"DROP_SHADOW\",color:{r:0,g:0,b:0,a:a},offset:{x:0,y:y},radius:r,visible:true,blendMode:\"NORMAL\"}];\n     function txt(ch,sz,st,col,w){const t=figma.createText();t.fontName={family:\"Poppins\",style:st};t.characters=ch;t.fontSize=sz;t.fills=[F(col)];if(w){t.textAutoResize=\"HEIGHT\";t.resize(w,t.height);}return t;}\n     const P={PLUS:\"M12 5 L12 19 M5 12 L19 12\",MINUS:\"M5 12 L19 12\",CLOSE:\"M5 5 L19 19 M19 5 L5 19\",CHD:\"M6 9 L12 15 L18 9\",CHL:\"M15 5 L8 12 L15 19\",CHR:\"M9 5 L16 12 L9 19\",FILTER:\"M4 7 L20 7 M7 12 L17 12 M10 17 L14 17\",SHARE:\"M12 3 L12 14 M8.5 6 L12 2.5 L15.5 6 M8 10 L6 10 L6 20 L18 20 L18 10 L16 10\",PENCIL:\"M4 20 L5 16 L15.5 5.5 L18.5 8.5 L8 19 L4 20 Z\",LOGOUT:\"M9 21 L5 21 L5 3 L9 3 M16 17 L21 12 L16 7 M21 12 L9 12\",STAR:\"M12 2 L14.9 8.2 L21.5 9 L16.6 13.6 L17.9 20.1 L12 16.9 L6.1 20.1 L7.4 13.6 L2.5 9 L9.1 8.2 L12 2 Z\"};\n     function icn(d,t,color,filled){const v=figma.createVector();v.vectorPaths=[{windingRule:filled?\"NONZERO\":\"NONE\",data:d}];if(filled){v.fills=[F(color)];v.strokes=[];}else{v.strokes=[F(color)];v.strokeWeight=2;v.strokeCap=\"ROUND\";v.strokeJoin=\"ROUND\";v.fills=[];}v.name=\"Icon\";const m=Math.max(v.width,v.height);const k=t/m;v.resize(v.width*k,v.height*k);return v;}\n     function recolor(n,hex){const c=[F(hex)];const walk=l=>{if([\"VECTOR\",\"ELLIPSE\",\"RECTANGLE\",\"BOOLEAN_OPERATION\",\"LINE\",\"STAR\"].indexOf(l.type)>=0){try{if(l.fills&&l.fills.length&&l.fills[0].visible!==false)l.fills=c;}catch(e){}try{if(l.strokes&&l.strokes.length&&l.strokes[0].visible!==false)l.strokes=c;}catch(e){}}if(l.type===\"TEXT\")l.fills=c;if(\"children\"in l){for(const k2 of l.children)walk(k2);}};walk(n);}\n     function mediaInst(name,parent){const m=MASTER[name].createInstance();parent.appendChild(m);return m;}\n     function fitIn(m,w,h){const s=Math.min(w/m.width,h/m.height);m.resize(m.width*s,m.height*s);}\n     ```\n     Frame-call helpers (from the rolled-back frames call, reuse with the findOne fix):\n     ```js\n     function mkFrame(name,x,y,w,h,bg){const f=figma.createFrame();WS.appendChild(f);f.x=x;f.y=y;f.resize(w,h);f.name=name;f.fills=[F(bg)];f.clipsContent=true;return f;}\n     function statusBar(parent,dark,transparent){const s=MASTER[\"Status Bar\"].createInstance();parent.appendChild(s);s.x=0;s.y=0;if(transparent)s.fills=[];else if(dark)s.fills=[F(C.dark)];recolor(s,dark?\"#FFFFFF\":\"#181725\");return s;}\n     function homeInd(parent,dark,transparent,y){const h=MASTER[\"Home Indicator\"].createInstance();parent.appendChild(h);h.x=0;h.y=(y===undefined?862:y);if(transparent)h.fills=[];else if(dark)h.fills=[F(C.dark)];recolor(h,dark?\"#FFFFFF\":\"#181725\");return h;}\n     function btn(parent,label,x,y,name){const b=MASTER[\"Button\"].createInstance();parent.appendChild(b);b.x=x;b.y=y;if(name)b.name=name;setTxt(b,label);return b;}\n     ```\n     NEW fix helpers to add (replace every `.findOne` usage):\n     ```js\n     function findN(n,fn){if(fn(n))return n;if(\"children\"in n){for(const k of n.children){const r=findN(k,fn);if(r)return r;}}return null;}\n     function findTxt(n){return findN(n,k=>k.type===\"TEXT\");}\n     function findByName(n,name){return findN(n,k=>k.name===name);}\n     const fails=[];\n     function setTxt(n,label){const t=findTxt(n);if(t)t.characters=label;else fails.push(label);return t;}\n     ```\n     Planned instance-override helpers for later frames (use findByName/findTxt):\n     ```js\n     function prodCard(parent,x,y,name,title,unit,price,imgName){const ci=MASTER[\"Product Card\"].createInstance();parent.appendChild(ci);ci.x=x;ci.y=y;if(name)ci.name=name;findByName(ci,\"Name\").characters=title;findByName(ci,\"Unit\").characters=unit;findByName(ci,\"Price\").characters=price;const p=findByName(ci,\"Photo\");p.swapComponent(MASTER[imgName]);const mw=MASTER[imgName].width,mh=MASTER[imgName].height;const s=Math.min(130/mw,80/mh);p.resize(mw*s,mh*s);p.x=(147-p.width)/2;p.y=(86-p.height)/2;return ci;}\n     function sechead(parent,y,title){const si=MASTER[\"Section Header\"].createInstance();parent.appendChild(si);si.x=24;si.y=y;setTxt(si,title);return si;}\n     function cartItem(parent,y,name,title,unit,price,imgName){/* like prodCard but Cart Item, x=24, fit 66 into 70 box, (70-w)/2 centering */}\n     function catCard(parent,x,y,name,title,img,tint){/* Category Card instance, fills=[F(tint)], Label text, Photo swap fit 120×112, x=(171-w)/2, y=14 */}\n     function catChip(parent,x,y,name,title,imgName,tint){/* Category Chip instance, tint, Label, Photo swap fit 40×40 at (12,12) */}\n     function chkRow(parent,y,label,value,opts){/* Checkout Row instance at x=24; Label; Value text (null→visible=false); opts.icon→ValueIcon.visible=true; opts.total→Value Bold 20 dark + Chevron/Divider visible=false */}\n     function tabInst(parent,active,y){const TB=findN(figma.root,n=>n.type===\"COMPONENT_SET\"&&n.name===\"Tab Bar\");const v=TB.children.find(c=>c.name===\"ActiveTab=\"+active);const inst=v.createInstance();parent.appendChild(inst);inst.x=0;inst.y=y;return inst;}\n     function hotspot(parent,name,x,y,w,h){const r=figma.createRectangle();parent.appendChild(r);r.x=x;r.y=y;r.resize(w,h);r.fills=[];r.name=name;return r;}\n     function link(src,dest,trigger){try{src.reactions=[{action:{type:\"NODE\",destinationId:dest.id,navigation:\"NAVIGATE\",transition:null,overlay:null},trigger:trigger||{type:\"CLICK\"}}];}catch(e){try{src.reactions=[{action:{type:\"NODE\",destinationId:dest.id,navigation:\"NAVIGATE\"},trigger:trigger||{type:\"CLICK\"}}];}catch(e2){}}}\n     ```\n\n   - **Frame position map** (414-wide columns at x=0/514/1028/1542; rows y=0/1000/2450): 01_Splash(0,0,414×896), 02_Onboarding(514,0), 03_Sign_In(1028,0), 04_Verification(1542,0), 05_Home(0,1000,414×1348 scrolling), 06_Product_Detail(514,1000), 07_Explore(1028,1000), 08_Beverages(1542,1000), 09_My_Cart(0,2450), 10_Checkout_Overlay(514,2450), 11_Order_Accepted(1028,2450), 12_Account(1542,2450).\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - **`figma.createNodeWithSvg: no such property`** (this session): the API doesn't exist in this environment. FIXED by building icons with `figma.createVector()` + `vectorPaths` using absolute-only path data (M/L/Z, no arcs); stroke-based icons use windingRule \"NONE\" + strokes, filled star uses \"NONZERO\" + fills. The failed call left a stray empty \"Add Button\" component — next call wiped all WS children first (`for(const ch of [...WS.children])ch.remove();`) then rebuilt.\n   - **`combineAsVariants: Grouped nodes must be in the same page as the parent`**: variant components were auto-created on figma.currentPage, not on page 7:2. FIXED by `WS.appendChild(v)` immediately after each `figma.createComponent()` before combining. IMPORTANT side-discovery: the failed call rolled back COMPLETELY (verification showed only 8 WS children; orphan search found 0), so the seven part-2 components had to be re-issued in a separate successful call.\n   - **`cannot set property 'characters' of null` at PLUGIN_1_SOURCE:45:33** (frames 01–04 call, ROLLED BACK — no frames exist): `.findOne(...)` on a Text Field instance returned null when overriding the label to \"Mobile Number\" (column 33 matches `.characters` after a ~30-char findOne chain). Debug dump CONFIRMED the masters DO have the text children (Button 6:29 → TEXT \"Get Started\" 6:30; Text Field 6:35 → TEXT \"Email\" 6:36 + FRAME \"Input\" 6:37 → RECTANGLE \"Underline\" 6:38), so the null is an instance-side findOne behavior issue. FIX IN PROGRESS: replace ALL `.findOne()` calls with manual recursion helpers (`findN`/`findTxt`/`findByName`) and use defensive `setTxt` that records failures into a `fails` array returned in the JSON instead of throwing.\n   - **`figma.getPageById: no such property`** (earlier): use `figma.getNodeById(\"7:2\")`.\n   - **\"Code executed with no return value\"** (earlier): always end with `return JSON.stringify(...)`.\n   - **Intermittent MCP rate-limit errors**: simply retry the identical call.\n   - **Input truncation on ~14k-char use_figma calls** (earlier session): keep calls ≲8k chars; build in sections.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Full design system established: brand #53B175, dark #181725, gray #7C7C7C, light #B1B1B1, border #E2E2E2, surface #F2F3F2, white, rating/offer orange #F3603F, FB blue #1877F2; Poppins Regular/Medium/SemiBold/Bold; radii 19 buttons/18 cards/15 search/24 sheet; card shadow SH(4,16,0.06), circle SH(2,10,0.12), tab bar SH(-4,16,0.05), sheet SH(-4,24,0.15); 24px margins, 366px content width, 24px column gap (columns x24/x219).\n   - Component library (16 items) fully created and verified in 03 · Workspace.\n   - Cover-crop technique for photos: clipping frame + instance scaled by `Math.max(targetW/w, targetH/h)` centered.\n   - Icon strategy resolved after createNodeWithSvg unavailable: vectorPaths-based `icn()` helper with per-path geometry scaling to target max-dimension.\n   - Prototype plan: reactions set directly on named nodes (buttons, cards, hotspots) — transparent hotspot rects over tab-bar tab regions (82.8 wide each at x=0/82.8/165.6/248.4/331.2, height 84) for tab navigation; splash AFTER_DELAY; flowStartingPoint \"Nectar Shopper\" in try/catch.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - \"请在以下Figma文件中完成完整设计： Figma 文件：https://www.figma.com/design/aBJm2MvkIZqCV7cu0O7PHX/ 请先阅读「00·Start Here」中的设计任务，参考「01· Foundations」中的视觉规范，复用「02·Components」中的组件，使用「04·Media」中的素材，最终将完整设计交付至「03·Workspace」。\" (the only real user message; everything else is system/task framing and continuation instructions).\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Re-issue frames 01_Splash, 02_Onboarding, 03_Sign_In, 04_Verification with the findN/setTxt fix (call rolled back).\n   - Build 05_Home (414×1348, call 3).\n   - Build 06_Product_Detail + 07_Explore (call 4); 08_Beverages + 09_My_Cart (call 5); 10_Checkout_Overlay + 11_Order_Accepted + 12_Account (call 6).\n   - Wire ALL prototype reactions + flow start (call 7).\n   - Screenshot-verify all 12 frames (get_screenshot), fix visible issues, re-verify.\n   - Final answer with file URL, page ID 7:2, screen IDs, prototype summary, limitations.\n\n8. Current Work:\n   Immediately before this summary: the frames 01–04 use_figma call failed with `TypeError: cannot set property 'characters' of null at <anonymous> (PLUGIN_1_SOURCE:45:33)` and ROLLED BACK (no frames exist). The failing line was an instance text override — most likely `pf.findOne(n=>n.type===\"TEXT\").characters=\"Mobile Number\";` on the Text Field instance named \"Tap/Phone\" (or equivalently a findOne on the Social Button \"Label\"). I then ran a read-only debug call dumping the Button and Text Field masters, which returned:\n   ```json\n   [{\"n\":\"Button\",\"t\":\"COMPONENT\",\"id\":\"6:29\",\"ch\":[{\"n\":\"Get Started\",\"t\":\"TEXT\",\"id\":\"6:30\"}]},\n    {\"n\":\"Text Field\",\"t\":\"COMPONENT\",\"id\":\"6:35\",\"ch\":[{\"n\":\"Email\",\"t\":\"TEXT\",\"id\":\"6:36\"},{\"n\":\"Input\",\"t\":\"FRAME\",\"id\":\"6:37\",\"ch\":[{\"n\":\"Underline\",\"t\":\"RECTANGLE\",\"id\":\"6:38\"}]}]}]\n   ```\n   confirming the text children exist on the masters, so the fix is to stop relying on `.findOne` for instance traversal and use manual recursion with defensive null handling. The frames 01–04 build code itself was otherwise sound (Splash: dark bg, Status Bar recolored white, Nectar_Logo_White resized 240×60 at (87,418); Onboarding: transparent status bar, 414×560 Hero with Photo_Welcome_Delivery cover + vertical gradient rect (GRADIENT_LINEAR, transform [[0,1,0],[-1,0,1]], stops a:0→a:0.85), texts at y604/y652, Button instance \"Btn/Get Started\" (25,753), transparent HI; Sign_In: photo hero 414×280 at y44, title y356, Text Field instance \"Tap/Phone\" (24,470) label→\"Mobile Number\", Flag_Bangladesh 30×18 (24,505), \"+880\" (64,503), divider 1×24 (116,502), \"Or connect with social media\" centered y618 with side hairlines, Social Button instances \"Btn/Google\" (25,664) and \"Btn/Facebook\" (25,747, label→\"Continue with Facebook\", nested SocialIcon swapped to Icon_Facebook_White recolored #1877F2 refit (28, centered); Verification: Circle Button \"Btn/Back\" (24,64) + CHL vector 18 centered, \"Enter your 4-digit code\" 24 SemiBold (24,140), Code Input instance (24,210), \"Resend Code\" 18 SemiBold brand (24,788), Next FAB frame 67×67 radius 33.5 brand (323,779) \"Btn/Next\" with CHR 20 white centered, HI).\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Re-issue the frames 01–04 call exactly as before but with the traversal fix: add `findN`/`findTxt`/`findByName`/`setTxt` (fails array) helpers and replace every `.findOne(...)` usage (Text Field label \"Mobile Number\", btn() label setter, Social Button label/icon overrides) with them; return `{ids, fails}` so any silent override failure is visible. This directly continues the rolled-back work — the last assistant action before the debug dump was the failed call \"Build frames 01_Splash, 02_Onboarding, 03_Sign_In, 04_Verification\", and the immediately preceding assistant message stated: \"The Text Field instance lookup returned no text child — the call rolled back. Let me inspect the actual Text Field component structure first.\" After frames 01–04 succeed, proceed to 05_Home, then 06/07, 08/09, 10/11/12, then prototype wiring, then screenshot verification of all 12 frames.\n\n   Detail