{"type":"assistant","message":{"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Labels repaired. Now build frames 01–04 with the safe traversal helpers (manual recursion, no reliance on findOne semantics — though probe showed findOne works fine on Text Field instance; the real bug was the missing Label, which is now fixed).\n\nActually since the root cause was missing children (not findOne), findOne is safe again. But I'll keep manual recursion helpers anyway — harmless and robust.\n\nNow re-issue the frames 01–04 call. Recall the plan:\n\n**01_Splash** (0,0,414×896): dark bg #181725; Status Bar instance transparent fills, recolored white; Nectar_Logo_White instance resized 240×60 at (87,418); Home Indicator transparent, recolored white.\n\n**02_Onboarding** (514,0): Status Bar transparent recolored dark; Hero frame 414×560 at y0 clipsContent with Photo_Welcome_Delivery cover-cropped + gradient scrim rect (GRADIENT_LINEAR transform [[0,1,0],[-1,0,1]], stops transparent→black 0.85) — actually gradient vertical from transparent top to dark bottom; texts: \"Get your groceries in as fast as one hour\" — wait no. Onboarding: title \"Welcome to our store\" 32 SemiBold white centered at y604, subtitle \"Get your groceries in as fast as one hour\" 16 Medium gray centered y652? Per nectar design: big white title on photo? Actually the classic nectar onboarding: photo hero top, then dark bg below with \"Welcome to our store\" white 32 centered... Let me follow my earlier plan from summary: \"texts at y604/y652, Button instance 'Btn/Get Started' (25,753), transparent HI\". The frame bg below hero is dark #181725? The nectar onboarding has dark background below the photo. Title \"Welcome to our store\" white 32 SemiBold at y604, subtitle \"Get your groceries in as fast as one hour\" gray #FCFCFC 70% or gray 16 Medium at y652.\n\nWait — but actually the gradient: hero photo with gradient at bottom. And title INSIDE hero? No — hero is 414×560, title at y604 is below hero on frame bg. Frame bg dark #181725. That matches classic design.\n\n**03_Sign_In** (1028,0): white bg; Status Bar dark; photo hero 414×280 at y44 (Photo_Sign_In_Groceries cover); title \"Get your groceries with nectar\" 26 SemiBold dark at (24,356) w366? Actually title centered? Nectar design: left-aligned. I'll use (24,356) 26 SemiBold dark w366. Text Field instance \"Tap/Phone\" at (24,470) — wait, Text Field is 364×76 with label \"Email\" at top and underline. Label override → \"Mobile Number\". Then Flag_Bangladesh 30×18 at (24,505)? Hmm — inside the text field, the input row: the flag + +880 sit on the underline row. Text Field component: label at y0 (16 SemiBold), Input frame at y24 (364×40) containing underline rect at bottom y40. So flag at (24, 470+24+~10) = (24, 504), \"+880\" 16 Medium dark at (64,502), divider 1×24 at (116,502) light gray.\n\nHmm wait, but flag height 18 at y505; +880 text at y503 16 Medium. OK per plan.\n\nThen \"Or connect with social media\" 14 Medium gray centered y618 with side hairlines (each ~120×1 #E2E2E2 at y~626): l1 x24 w120, l2 x270 w120. Social Button \"Btn/Google\" (25,664) default label; \"Btn/Facebook\" (25,747) label→\"Continue with Facebook\", SocialIcon swap→Icon_Facebook_White recolored #1877F2 refit 24 at (28, centered). Home Indicator.\n\n**04_Verification** (1542,0): white bg; Status Bar; Circle Button \"Btn/Back\" (24,64) 44×44 with CHL vector 18 dark centered (child of the instance? Adding a vector as child of an instance — allowed, instances accept children). Wait — can I append children to an INSTANCE? Yes, instances allow appending children (they become overrides). Good.\n- \"Enter your 4-digit code\" 24 SemiBold dark at (24,140) w366? It's two lines: \"Enter your\\n4-digit code\" — plan says (24,140). I'll set w 250 so it wraps naturally? Actually exact copy \"Enter your 4-digit code\". Let me set textAutoResize HEIGHT w250 at (24,140).\n- Code Input instance (24,210).\n- \"Resend Code\" 18 SemiBold brand (24,788).\n- Next FAB: frame 67×67 radius 33.5 brand at (323,779) name \"Btn/Next\" with CHR vector 20 white centered inside.\n- Home Indicator.\n\nAlso per navigation: 03 phone field→04 — link on the Text Field instance (or a hotspot over it). I'll add hotspot later in prototype wiring; better: name instances for lookup. I'll name: f3's text field \"Tap/Phone\".\n\nAlso 04 back→03, next→05 (wired later via Btn/Back and Btn/Next lookups).\n\nSplash AFTER_DELAY wiring later.\n\nFonts: Poppins Regular/Medium/SemiBold/Bold all loaded.\n\nNow write the full call. Keep ≤ ~8-9k chars. Let me write compactly.\n\n```js\nawait Promise.all([\"Regular\",\"Medium\",\"SemiBold\",\"Bold\"].map(s=>figma.loadFontAsync({family:\"Poppins\",style:s})));\nconst WS=figma.getNodeById(\"7:2\");\nconst F=(hex,o)=>{o=o===undefined?1:o;const n=parseInt(hex.slice(1),16);return{type:\"SOLID\",color:{r:((n>>16)&255)/255,g:((n>>8)&255)/255,b:(n&255)/255},opacity:o};};\nconst C={brand:\"#53B175\",dark:\"#181725\",gray:\"#7C7C7C\",light:\"#B1B1B1\",border:\"#E2E2E2\",surface:\"#F2F3F2\",white:\"#FFFFFF\",fb:\"#1877F2\"};\nconst MASTER={};for(const c of figma.root.findAllWithCriteria({types:[\"COMPONENT\"]}))MASTER[c.name]=c;\nfunction findN(n,fn){if(fn(n))return n;if(\"children\"in n){for(const k of n.children){const r=findN(k,fn);if(r)return r;}}return null;}\nfunction findTxt(n){return findN(n,k=>k.type===\"TEXT\");}\nfunction findByName(n,name){return findN(n,k=>k.name===name);}\nconst fails=[];\nfunction setTxt(n,label){const t=findTxt(n);if(t)t.characters=label;else fails.push(label);return t;}\nfunction txt(ch,sz,st,col,w){const t=figma.createText();t.fontName={family:\"Poppins\",style:st};t.characters=ch;t.fontSize=sz;t.fills=[F(col)];if(w){t.textAutoResize=\"HEIGHT\";t.resize(w,t.height);}return t;}\nconst P={CHL:\"M15 5 L8 12 L15 19\",CHR:\"M9 5 L16 12 L9 19\"};\nfunction icn(d,t,color){const v=figma.createVector();v.vectorPaths=[{windingRule:\"NONE\",data:d}];v.strokes=[F(color)];v.strokeWeight=2;v.strokeCap=\"ROUND\";v.strokeJoin=\"ROUND\";v.fills=[];v.name=\"Icon\";const m=Math.max(v.width,v.height);const k=t/m;v.resize(v.width*k,v.height*k);return v;}\nfunction recolor(n,hex){const c=[F(hex)];const walk=l=>{if(l.type===\"VECTOR\"||l.type===\"ELLIPSE\"||l.type===\"RECTANGLE\"||l.type===\"BOOLEAN_OPERATION\"||l.type===\"LINE\"){try{if(l.fills&&l.fills.length&&l.fills[0].visible!==false)l.fills=c;}catch(e){}try{if(l.strokes&&l.strokes.length&&l.strokes[0].visible!==false)l.strokes=c;}catch(e){}}if(l.type===\"TEXT\")l.fills=c;if(\"children\"in l){for(const k2 of l.children)walk(k2);}};walk(n);}\nfunction mediaInst(name,parent){const m=MASTER[name].createInstance();parent.appendChild(m);return m;}\nfunction mkFrame(name,x,y,w,h,bg){const f=figma.createFrame();WS.appendChild(f);f.x=x;f.y=y;f.resize(w,h);f.name=name;f.fills=[F(bg)];f.clipsContent=true;return f;}\nfunction statusBar(parent,white){const s=MASTER[\"Status Bar\"].createInstance();parent.appendChild(s);s.x=0;s.y=0;s.fills=[];recolor(s,white?\"#FFFFFF\":\"#181725\");return s;}\nfunction homeInd(parent,white,y){const h=MASTER[\"Home Indicator\"].createInstance();parent.appendChild(h);h.x=0;h.y=(y===undefined?862:y);h.fills=[];recolor(h,white?\"#FFFFFF\":\"#181725\");return h;}\nfunction btn(parent,label,x,y,name){const b=MASTER[\"Button\"].createInstance();parent.appendChild(b);b.x=x;b.y=y;if(name)b.name=name;setTxt(b,label);return b;}\nfunction cover(parent,imgName,x,y,w,h,name){const fr=figma.createFrame();parent.appendChild(fr);fr.x=x;fr.y=y;fr.resize(w,h);fr.clipsContent=true;fr.fills=[];if(name)fr.name=name;const m=mediaInst(imgName,fr);const s=Math.max(w/m.width,h/m.height);m.resize(m.width*s,m.height*s);m.x=(w-m.width)/2;m.y=(h-m.height)/2;return fr;}\nconst ids={};\n// 01 Splash\nconst f1=mkFrame(\"01_Splash\",0,0,414,896,C.dark);ids.f1=f1.id;\nstatusBar(f1,true);\nconst lg=mediaInst(\"Nectar_Logo_White\",f1);lg.resize(240,60);lg.x=87;lg.y=418;\nhomeInd(f1,true);\n// 02 Onboarding\nconst f2=mkFrame(\"0