idth 28 — Icon_Payment master is 24×17).\n\nAlso v.characters: need fonts loaded (fine in build call).\n\nAlso for Payment row: v.visible=false works (vvis ok). Then overlay Icon_Payment instance recolored dark, fit ~28×19 at sheet coords (302, 154+34=188). ValueIcon x=278,y=34,w=28,h=19. Icon_Payment 24×17 → scale to fit 28×19: s=min(28/24,19/17)=min(1.166,1.117)=1.117 → 26.8×19. Place centered in that 28×19 box: x=278+(28-26.8)/2=278.6, y=34. As sibling in sheet: x=24+278.6=302.6, y=154+34=188.\n\nHmm wait, but actually should the Payment icon appear at the value position? Yes — in the nectar design, Payment row shows a payment-card icon on the right instead of text.\n\nSimpler alternative: build all 4 rows as custom frames. But rows as instances preserve component reuse (benchmark wants component reuse). The other 3 rows work fine with text overrides. Only Payment needs the sibling icon.\n\nAlso check: Chevron visible toggle for Total row — Chevron is a VECTOR in master, present in instance (kids show Chevron:VECTOR). Divider RECTANGLE present. Good — visibility toggles should work on those (they're not instances).\n\nAlso Label: findTxt(r) returns first TEXT = Label. Its font: Label is 18 SemiBold per master dump (fontSize 18). Fine with loaded fonts.\n\nValue: 16 Medium. Fine.\n\nFor Total row: v.fontSize=20, v.fontName Bold — font overrides on instance text OK.\n\nOne more check from the probe: Value characters write needs font loaded — in build we load all four styles first. Good.\n\nNow rewrite the build with:\n- chkRow without ValueIcon handling\n- Payment icon sibling overlay\n\nAlso note: `kids` in probe shows the instance prunes the nested invisible INSTANCE (ValueIcon). Interesting quirk. Also means in Cart Item instances the Stepper (nested instance, visible) is present — fine, we don't use Cart Item instances anyway.\n\nNow the full build call for 10+11 again, modified. Also keep in mind: for Payment row, hide v (Value text). Chevron stays visible (fine, matches design? In nectar design, Payment row has icon not chevron... Actually original design shows a card icon on right. Chevron at x346 would remain. Looking at the reference: Payment row right side shows credit-card icon. I'll hide Chevron for payment row too and place icon at ~x346? Hmm. ValueIcon at x278 — that's mid-right, with Chevron at 346 to its right. Design-wise: icon + chevron side by side. Keep chevron, add icon at 278-ish. That matches master layout intent (ValueIcon 28 wide at 278, chevron at 346).\n\nWrite the call now. Reuse preamble, modified chkRow:\n\n```js\nfunction chkRow(parent,x,y,label,value,opts){const r=MASTER[\"Checkout Row\"].createInstance();parent.appendChild(r);r.x=x;r.y=y;findTxt(r).characters=label;const v=findN(r,n=>n.name===\"Value\"&&n.type===\"TEXT\");if(value){v.characters=value;}else{v.visible=false;}if(opts&&opts.total){v.fontSize=20;v.fontName={family:\"Poppins\",style:\"Bold\"};v.fills=[F(C.dark)];const cv=findN(r,n=>n.name===\"Chevron\");cv.visible=false;const dv=findN(r,n=>n.name===\"Divider\");dv.visible=false;}return r;}\n```\n\nAnd for payment: after chkRow(sheet,24,154,\"Payment\",null,{}), add icon:\n```js\nconst pi=mediaInst(\"Icon_Payment\",sheet);recolor(pi,C.dark);const ps=Math.min(28/pi.width,19/pi.height);pi.resize(pi.width*ps,pi.height*ps);pi.x=24+278+(28-pi.width)/2;pi.y=154+34+(19-pi.height)/2;\n```\nIcon_Payment master 24×17 → ps=min(28/24,19/17)=1.117→ 26.8×19. x=24+278+0.6=302.6, y=188.\n\nOK, full call.","signature":"42483be7e51e47eda2022a67"}],"id":"6d412ad1-29af-46e7-9e4a-b1ee452c8e48","model":"glm-5.3-flash","role":"assistant","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b3eb8a6a-7ab8-425f-a694-fe8d0804e2da","uuid":"3eef98c3-dc6e-4a56-9214-c42b2fcc4c66","timestamp":"2026-10-30T22:07:19.375Z","thinking_duration_ms":31197}
