{"type":"assistant","message":{"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"All 12 frames built:\n- 01_Splash = 18:2\n- 02_Onboarding = 18:30\n- 03_Sign_In = 18:51\n- 04_Verification = 18:95\n- 05_Home = 19:2\n- 06_Product_Detail = 20:2\n- 07_Explore = 20:52\n- 08_Beverages = 21:2\n- 09_My_Cart = 21:69\n- 10_Checkout_Overlay = 25:2\n- 11_Order_Accepted = 25:102\n- 12_Account = 26:4\n\nNow prototype wiring. Navigation rules:\n- 01_Splash auto AFTER_DELAY 2000 → 02; flowStartingPoint \"Nectar Shopper\"\n- 02 Get Started → 03\n- 03 phone field → 04 (link the Text Field instance \"Tap/Phone\")\n- 04 back → 03 (Btn/Back circle), next → 05 (Btn/Next)\n- 05 Red Apple card → 06 (\"Card/Red Apple\"), tabs: Explore→07, Cart→09, Account→12 (hotspots Tap/Explore, Tap/Cart, Tap/Account)\n- 06 back → 05 (Btn/Back), Add To Basket → 09 (Btn/Add To Basket)\n- 07 Beverages card → 08 (\"Card/Beverages\"), tabs: Shop→05, Cart→09, Account→12 (Tap/Shop, Tap/Cart, Tap/Account)\n- 08 back → 07 (Btn/Back)\n- 09 Go to Checkout → 10 (Btn/Go to Checkout), tabs: Shop→05, Explore→07, Account→12 (Tap/Shop, Tap/Explore, Tap/Account)\n- 10 close → 09 (Btn/Close), Place Order → 11 (Btn/Place Order)\n- 11 Back to home → 05 (Btn/Back to home)\n- 12 tabs: Shop→05, Explore→07, Cart→09 (Tap/Shop, Tap/Explore, Tap/Cart)\n\nNavigation for overlay 10: it should open OVER 09. In prototype terms: since 10 is a full frame containing cart behind, plain NAVIGATE works. The brief says \"10_Checkout_Overlay opens over 09 (cart visible behind)\". Options: (a) Navigate 09→10 (simple); (b) OVERLAY with 10 as overlay... but 10 is a full 414×896 frame; overlay presentation requires the frame to be an overlay over 09 — with a transparent... no, 10 is opaque with scrim + sheet. If presented as OVERLAY over 09, the cart behind would be 09's actual content — that matches \"cart visible behind\"! With scrim 0.4 and sheet, the overlay shows through to 09.\n\nBut overlay presentation: reactions action {type:\"NODE\", destinationId, navigation:\"OVERLAY\", overlay:{...}}? Overlay action requires overlay presentation settings. The schema: action {type:\"NODE\", destinationId, navigation:\"OVERLAY\", overlay:{type:\"MANUAL\", ...}}? Hmm — overlay positioning. And the overlay frame needs background transparent? 10 has white fill + full-size scrim + sheet — as overlay it renders above 09 fully covering it. The scrim 0.4 lets 09 show through. That's exactly \"opens over 09 with cart visible behind\".\n\nBut there's risk: overlay API details (overlay:{overlayPositionType:\"CENTER\"} etc.) may not be supported in this env; and close (Btn/Close → 09) would need navigation \"CLOSE\"/\"BACK\" instead of NAVIGATE. The brief says \"10 close→09\". Simpler and safer: plain NAVIGATE both ways (09→10 navigate, 10 close→09 navigate). The visual result is the same since 10 already renders the cart behind the scrim. The brief's \"opens over 09 (cart visible behind)\" is satisfied visually by the baked-in cart content. Given env quirks, I'll use NAVIGATE with transition null. Also prototype \"close\" as navigation:\"CLOSE\" only works for overlays; NAVIGATE to 09 is fine.\n\nHmm — but should I try overlay for fidelity? The brief in 00·Start Here (from summary): \"10_Checkout_Overlay opens over 09 (cart visible behind); → Place Order → 11\". A plain navigate from 09 to 10 still shows 10 with cart behind scrim — visually identical. I'll do NAVIGATE. Note it in final limitations if needed.\n\nLink helper with reactions. Also AFTER_DELAY for splash. flowStartingPoint try/catch.\n\nLink list (by frame name → node names):\n- f1 18:2: auto → f2 (AFTER_DELAY 2000); flowStartingPoint\n- f2 18:30: \"Btn/Get Started\" → f3\n- f3 18:51: \"Tap/Phone\" (Text Field instance) → f4\n- f4 18:95: \"Btn/Back\" → f3; \"Btn/Next\" → f5\n- f5 19:2: \"Card/Red Apple\" → f6; \"Tap/Explore\" → f7; \"Tap/Cart\" → f9; \"Tap/Account\" → f12\n- f6 20:2: \"Btn/Back\" → f5; \"Btn/Add To Basket\" → f9\n- f7 20:52: \"Card/Beverages\" → f8; \"Tap/Shop\" → f5; \"Tap/Cart\" → f9; \"Tap/Account\" → f12\n- f8 21:2: \"Btn/Back\" → f7\n- f9 21:69: \"Btn/Go to Checkout\" → f10; \"Tap/Shop\" → f5; \"Tap/Explore\" → f7; \"Tap/Account\" → f12\n- f10 25:2: \"Btn/Close\" → f9; \"Btn/Place Order\" → f11\n- f11 25:102: \"Btn/Back to home\" → f5\n- f12 26:4: \"Tap/Shop\" → f5; \"Tap/Explore\" → f7; \"Tap/Cart\" → f9\n\nFind target nodes by name within each frame: findByName(frame, name). For f3 \"Tap/Phone\": the Text Field instance — was it named \"Tap/Phone\"? From summary: 'Text Field instance \"Tap/Phone\" (24,470)'. Yes.\n\nNames to link are all named nodes. Note: in f5 the card is named \"Card/Red Apple\", f7 \"Card/Beverages\". Buttons: f2 \"Btn/Get Started\" (Button instance named). f4: \"Btn/Back\" circle instance, \"Btn/Next\" custom frame. f6: \"Btn/Back\", \"Btn/Add To Basket\". f8: \"Btn/Back\". f9: \"Btn/Go to Checkout\". f10: \"Btn/Close\" (vector), \"Btn/Place Order\". f11: \"Btn/Back to home\". Hotspots named \"Tap/*\".\n\nWrite the wiring call. Use link() with try/catch fallback. Also set flowStartingPoint on f1.\n\nOne call, return list of links applied + any failures.","signature":"a48d33f0a85e4e48aa7f15f8"}],"id":"7d47f154-3306-404e-becf-0d1fdd4d8691","model":"glm-5.3-flash","role":"assistant","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b3eb8a6a-7ab8-425f-a694-fe8d0804e2da","uuid":"1dd7ae3e-2112-44e1-bc53-b475b5349a92","timestamp":"2026-10-30T22:09:42.019Z","thinking_duration_ms":26028}
