{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\n<tools-used-before-summary>mcp__figma__get_metadata, mcp__figma__get_screenshot, mcp__figma__use_figma, mcp__figma__whoami</tools-used-before-summary>\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   Complete an unattended Figma product design benchmark. Assigned file: https://www.figma.com/design/aBJm2MvkIZqCV7cu0O7PHX/ (fileKey `aBJm2MvkIZqCV7cu0O7PHX`). Original user request (Chinese, the only real user message): Read the design task in「00·Start Here」, follow visual specs in「01·Foundations」, reuse components from「02·Components」, use assets from「04·Media」, and deliver the complete design to「03·Workspace」.\n\n   Binding constraints (system/task instructions):\n   - Account confirmed as huangxinyue@tetras.ai (whoami called in session 1).\n   - Use ONLY this assigned file; preserve all reference pages (`0:1` 00·Start Here, `1:2` 01·Foundations, `1:3` 02·Components, `1:4` 04·Media) and their nodes; do not create a different file or switch accounts/teams.\n   - Create everything inside 03 · Workspace (page `7:2`); new frames, reusable components and prototype connections allowed there. Starter read-only instructions apply to preserving reference pages, not the workspace.\n   - Before EVERY tool call include a concise visible decision summary prefixed exactly `Reasoning summary:` in the same assistant message; after each tool result do the same. Final response: first line `Reasoning summary: ...`, then `Final answer:` with the assigned file URL, the 03 · Workspace page ID, screen IDs, prototype work completed, and remaining limitations. Never claim completion for unfinished work.\n   - Load fonts before editing text; valid Plugin API only; NEVER use loadAllPagesAsync, setPluginData, createImageAsync (createNodeWithSvg also doesn't exist).\n   - Build in manageable sections; verify with get_screenshot; finish screens + states + prototype flows before final answer. Unattended session — resolve routine choices from the brief without waiting. Keep calls ≲8k chars to avoid input truncation.\n\n   Product brief (from 00 · Start Here, binding): \"Nectar\" online groceries app, canvas 414×896, light mode, exactly 12 frames with exact names, wired as a clickable prototype. Fixed data/copy (verbatim, brief wins over source-kit typos):\n   - Shopper: Afsar Hossen · imshuvo97@gmail.com · avatar = Avatar_Neutral · Location: Dhaka, Banasree · phone +880 (Flag_Bangladesh) · unit format \"1kg, Price\"\n   - Catalog (name · size · price · image master): Organic Bananas · 7pcs · $4.99 · Product_Organic_Bananas; Red Apple · 1kg · $4.99 · Product_Red_Apple (detail title \"Natural Red Apple\"); Bell Pepper Red · 1kg · $4.99 · Product_Bell_Pepper_Red; Ginger · 250gm · $2.99 · Product_Ginger; Beef Bone · 1kg · $4.99 · Product_Beef_Bone; Broiler Chicken · 1kg · $4.99 · Product_Broiler_Chicken; Egg Chicken Red · 4pcs · $1.99 · Product_Egg_Chicken_Red\n   - Beverages: Diet Coke · 355ml · $1.99; Sprite Can · 325ml · $1.50; Apple & Grape Juice · 2L · $15.99; Orange Juice · 2L · $15.99; Coca Cola Can · 325ml · $4.99; Pepsi Can · 330ml · $4.99\n   - Home: \"Dhaka, Banasree\"; search \"Search Store\"; Promotion \"Fresh Vegetables\" / \"Get Up To 40% OFF\" (Banner_Fresh_Vegetables); Exclusive Offer: Organic Bananas, Red Apple; Best Selling: Bell Pepper Red, Ginger; Groceries: categories Pulses (Category_Pulses), Rice (Category_Rice); products Beef Bone, Broiler Chicken\n   - Product detail: \"Natural Red Apple\" · \"1kg, Price\" · qty 1 · $4.99; description exactly: \"Apples are nutritious. Apples may be good for weight loss. Apples may be good for your heart. As part of a healthful and varied diet.\"; Nutritions 100gr; Review 5 of 5 stars\n   - Cart/checkout: Bell Pepper Red $4.99 · Egg Chicken Red $1.99 · Organic Bananas $4.99 · Ginger $2.99, qty 1 each, Total $14.96 everywhere (NOT $12.96/$13.97); Delivery \"Select Method\" · Promo Code \"Pick discount\"; legal \"By placing an order you agree to our Terms And Conditions\"\n   - Explore: \"Find Products\"; search \"Search Store\"; 6 categories: Fresh Fruits & Vegetable, Cooking Oil & Ghee, Meat & Fish, Bakery & Snacks, Dairy & Eggs, Beverages (images Category_*)\n   - Sign in: \"Get your groceries with nectar\" · +880 · \"Or connect with social media\" · Continue with Google · Continue with Facebook; Verification: \"Enter your 4-digit code\" · \"Code\" · Resend Code (4 digits, none entered); Onboarding: \"Welcome to our store\" · \"Get your groceries in as fast as one hour\" · Get Started; Accepted: \"Your Order has been accepted\" · \"Your items have been placed and are on their way to being processed\" · Track Order · Back to home\n   - Account: Afsar Hossen · imshuvo97@gmail.com; entries Orders · My Details · Delivery Address · Payment Methods · Promo Code · Notifications · Help · About · Log Out\n\n   Navigation rules: Main nav (Tab Bar) on frames 05, 07, 09, 12 — five tabs Shop(Icon_Shop)→05, Explore(Icon_Explore)→07, Cart(Icon_Cart)→09, Favourite(entry only, no link), Account(Icon_Account)→12; current tab must match frame. Pushed screens with back: 04 (→03), 06 (→05), 08 (→07); 06 & 08 have NO main nav. 10_Checkout_Overlay opens over 09 (cart visible behind — implemented as full frame with baked-in cart content behind 40% scrim + bottom sheet; plain NAVIGATE used); → Place Order → 11. Entry-only (NO links): See all, add to cart, share, favourite, filter, Resend Code, social sign-in buttons, Track Order, Favourite tab, Delivery/Payment/Promo rows, account entries, edit name, Log Out. NO extra frames beyond the 12. Frame links: 01_Splash auto(AFTER_TIMEOUT 2000)→02; 02 Get Started→03; 03 phone field→04; 04 back→03, next→05; 05 Red Apple card→06, tabs; 06 back→05, Add To Basket→09; 07 Beverages card→08, tabs; 08 back→07; 09 Go to Checkout→10, tabs; 10 close→09, Place Order→11; 11 Back to home→05; 12 tabs. Flow start on 01_Splash (named \"Nectar Shopper\").\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Figma Plugin API via `mcp__figma__use_figma` (code ≤50000 chars; MUST end with `return JSON.stringify(...)`); failed calls are TRANSACTIONAL (all changes roll back).\n   - **CRITICAL (this session): STALE VIEW TRAP — every use_figma call touching workspace nodes MUST begin with `await figma.setCurrentPageAsync(figma.getNodeById(\"7:2\"));`**. While currentPage was 0:1 (the desktop app's viewed page), getNodeById reported all workspace frames \"GONE\" and WS.children listed only components; after switching to 7:2 everything reappeared (frames had persisted all along). A PERSIST_TEST rect created after switching persisted and was then removed, confirming writes persist when the page is active.\n   - **Reaction schema in THIS environment (differs from standard docs)**: `node.reactions=[{actions:[{type:\"NODE\",destinationId,navigation:\"NAVIGATE\",transition:null}],trigger:{type:\"ON_CLICK\"}}]` — plural `actions` ARRAY (not singular `action`), trigger type \"ON_CLICK\" (not \"CLICK\"), auto-delay trigger `{type:\"AFTER_TIMEOUT\",timeout:2000}` (not AFTER_DELAY/delay), and NO `overlay` key in the action. This final form validated: all 26 links \"ok\".\n   - **`flowStartingPoint` does NOT exist in this environment** — probed `flowStartingPoint`/`flowStartingPoints` on frame, on page, `prototypeStartNode`: all false; assignment errors \"no such property\". Flow start cannot be set programmatically → report as limitation.\n   - **Instances PRUNE hidden nested instances**: Checkout Row master contains ValueIcon (nested INSTANCE, visible=false) but created instances have children only [Label, Value, Chevron, Divider]. Workaround: sibling overlay icons positioned in parent-frame coordinates.\n   - Instance child overrides allowed: text `characters` (requires that text's font loaded — Value is Poppins Medium; loading Regular/Medium/SemiBold/Bold up front covers it), `visible` toggles, `fontSize`/`fontName`/`fills` on text, `swapComponent()` (preserves instance size), `resize()` (keeps x,y top-left), `fills`. PROHIBITED: setting x/y or constraints on nodes nested inside instances (`relative-transform` / `vertical-constraint` errors).\n   - `figma.createVector()` + `vectorPaths` for icons (absolute M/L/Z only; windingRule \"NONE\"+strokes for line icons, \"NONZERO\"+fills for filled star).\n   - Fonts: Poppins Regular/Medium/SemiBold/Bold; Poppins style is \"SemiBold\" (no space).\n   - `figma.getNodeById` (NOT getPageById); MANUAL recursion helpers (findN/findTxt/findByName) instead of `.findOne`. Dump-helper gotcha hit twice: `dump(n,d)` with `if(\"children\"in n&&d<2)` called as dump(row,2) silently omits children — call with d=0.\n   - Intermittent MCP rate limits — retry the identical call.\n   - Custom frames built per-screen for anything needing per-item photo/icon positioning; component instances where overrides suffice.\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - **Figma file aBJm2MvkIZqCV7cu0O7PHX** — pages: `0:1`, `1:2`, `1:3`, `1:4`, `7:2` (03 · Workspace — delivery target, now contains 15 components + 12 frames; PERSIST_TEST removed).\n\n   - **FINAL FRAME ID MAP (all 12 verified present with correct contents)**:\n     - 01_Splash = `18:2` (0,0; dark #181725; Status Bar white; Nectar_Logo_White at (87,418); HI white)\n     - 02_Onboarding = `18:30` (514,0; hero 414×560 Photo_Welcome_Delivery + gradient scrim; \"Welcome to our store\" 32 SemiBold y604; \"Get your groceries in as fast as one hour\" 16 Medium #FCFCFC 0.7 y660; Button \"Btn/Get Started\" (25,753); HI dark)\n     - 03_Sign_In = `18:51` (1028,0; hero 414×280 y44 Photo_Sign_In_Groceries; \"Get your groceries with nectar\" 26 SemiBold (24,356); Text Field instance \"Tap/Phone\" (24,470) label→\"Mobile Number\"; Flag_Bangladesh (24,505); \"+880\" (64,503); divider (116,502); \"Or connect with social media\" y618 + hairlines; Soc