hevron? The Section Headers also have CHD? No — section headers use \"See all\" text only. The product detail has CHD at \"Product Detail\". In home, CHD was only for location.\n\nFix call: locate vector in 19:2 with parent===home (or in children of home) named \"Icon\" with y<140, set x/y. Then re-screenshot header region.\n\nActually wait — could the artifact instead be the carrot's leaf overlapping down? No, carrot bottom=90, artifact is at y~100+ mid-text. And shape looks like a \"V\" chevron. Also its x ~247: if I had placed CHD at (loc.x + 192 + 8)... loc.x=0 → 200? Hmm 247 could be from text w 239? Whatever.\n\nAlso double check \"Dhaka, Ba?asree\": the chevron overlaps \"n\". Move it right.\n\nCode:\n\n```js\nawait figma.setCurrentPageAsync(figma.getNodeById(\"7:2\"));\nconst home=figma.getNodeById(\"19:2\");\nconst R=[];\nfor(const k of home.children){ if(k.type===\"VECTOR\"&&k.y<140&&k.y>85){R.push({name:k.name,x:k.x,y:k.y,w:k.width,h:k.height}); k.x=308; k.y=104;} }\nreturn JSON.stringify(R);\n```\n\nBut careful: are there other top-level vectors in that y range? The search bar (instance) is not vector top-level. Banner at y199. Hotspots at y1230. So only the CHD should match y 85-140. If none found, search recursively for vectors with y between 90 and 130 whose parent is home... they'd be top-level anyway.\n\nWait — also possible: the chevron might be INSIDE a group/frame with the location text. I'll do recursive find for VECTOR with absolute y (via absoluteTransform? simpler: node.absoluteBoundingBox.y - home.absoluteBoundingBox.y between 90 and 130). Let me use absoluteBoundingBox to be safe.\n\n```js\nconst hb=home.absoluteBoundingBox;\nconst hits=[];\nfunction walk(n){ if(n.type===\"VECTOR\"){ const b=n.absoluteBoundingBox; const ry=b.y-hb.y; if(ry>88&&ry<135){hits.push({name:n.name,rx:b.x-hb.x,ry,rw:b.width,rh:b.height,id:n.id});}} if(\"children\"in n)for(const c of n.children)walk(c);}\nwalk(home);\n```\nThen for each hit, if it's not inside an instance (Search Bar is instance; its icon is inside instance at y~144+ — instance children can't be moved anyway; setting x on instance child errors → guard with try). Move to x=308, y=104 relative to home: n.x = 308 + (n.x - (b.x-hb.x)) ... simpler: n.x += (308 - (b.x-hb.x)); n.y += (104 - (b.y-hb.y)).\n\nHmm but the chevron should sit after text end. Text glyphs: \"Dhaka, Banasree\" centered, width ~192 → spans 111–303. Chevron 12 wide at x=309, vertically centered on the 27px text line: y = 96 + (27-12)/2 ≈ 103.5 → 104. But looking at typical nectar design, chevron is baseline-ish lower. y=104 fine.\n\nBut wait — if the chevron is a child of an INSTANCE (unlikely), the move errors and the whole call rolls back. Guard with try/catch per node.\n\nThen screenshot 19:2 again at 1348 to confirm, or screenshot at lower res 896 — the gap was visible at 896 too. Use 896.","signature":"cb2a3ff570fc4695a349633c"}],"id":"1a3adaff-9e84-465e-90e3-0b9bc098ed3e","model":"glm-5.3-flash","role":"assistant","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b3eb8a6a-7ab8-425f-a694-fe8d0804e2da","uuid":"8ec0cbe8-3898-4b72-804f-141118cd3205","timestamp":"2026-10-30T22:21:12.656Z","thinking_duration_ms":29821}
